window.SUPREME_MAGUS_CHAPTERS=(window.SUPREME_MAGUS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4501,"title":"Chapter 4501 Chaotic Mess (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"When your life force stabilizes and you can freely travel Mogar, however, I expect you to bring me souvenirs.\"","\"I will, Haug.\" Garrik nodded.","To make matters worse for the bartender, whenever the young Fomor discovered a new dish he liked, Ryla asked Haug to teach her the recipe.","\"I’m sorry to inconvenience you so often, Mister Haug.\" She sighed. \"It’s just that my son won’t be able to leave the Mansion for years, and while the Verhens are great cooks, I don’t think they’d enjoy so much exotic food.","\"I want to offer Garrik a bit more variety and let him experience Mogar, even if just by taste.\"","\"Don’t mention it as well, Ryla. Also, the ’drop the mister’ goes for you too.\" Haugh said with a smile that didn’t extend to his eyes.","’Here I am, spending too much time with a child that’s not mine and sharing my secret recipes with a woman I’m not going to date. Gods, if I feel like a total moron.’ He thought every time.","\"Mister... I mean, can I have a beer, Haug?\" Garrik asked, startling Ryla.","\"Of course.\" The bartender’s reply shocked her, but only until she turned to look at him and he winked. \"You are a kid, though, and deserve a kid’s glass.\"","Haug gave the young Fomor a shot of Maekosh beer, which Garrik downed in one gulp and spat back in the glass a second later.","\"Ewww! The bubbles feel nice, but it tastes bitter and burns!\" He said.","\"That’s why beer is an adult drink, young man.\" Haug replied. \"Maybe this is more to your taste. I call it Lemon Beer.\"","He served a full glass of a bubbly yellow liquid to Garrik and another to Ryla. It was a carbonated drink made from lemon juice, water to dilute it, and enough sugar to take off the sour edge.","\"It’s bubbly and delicious!\" The young Fomor said.","\"And it’s still beer.\" Haug winked at Ryla again, making her chuckle. \"Do you want it with your meals from now on?\"","\"Yes, please.\" Garrik nodded.","Meanwhile in the kitchen, the staff of the Travelling Tavern commented on the poor state of their employer’s affairs of the heart.","\"Poor sod.\" Vannir said. \"So much time wasted on a woman who turns into a monster at the drop of a hat.\"","\"How can you judge Ryla just from her appearance?\" Dryna snarled. \"Even in her monster form, she would still be the same wonderful person.\"","\"Yeah, right.\" Akkhar sneered. \"And I’m sure you dated Zelima in spite of her homely appearance.\"","He waved at the young cook who still looked lovely even with food and oil spots dirtying her work clothes and sweat drenching her hair.","\"Even better, point one woman in this room to me who dated a monster-ugly guy. Just one, and I’ll pile on Vannir with you.\"","The silence that followed was deafening.","\"My point exactly.\" Vannir nodded. \"Still, don’t get me wrong. I like the kid. Garrik treats us like heroes just because we share our stories with him. He doesn’t treat us like servants just because we serve at the tables.\"","\"He’s such a cute and polite boy.\" Zelima said with dreamy eyes. \"Do you think we should help Haug?\"","\"Help how?\" Kanlen shrugged. \"He’s a big man. Whatever he decides, he’s the one who has to live with it. I’d rather not mess up the already chaotic mess he’s in. If Haug needs advice, he’ll ask for it. But not from Vannir.\"","\"It’s too bad Haug turned you down, Van.\" Dryna suppressed a chortle. \"You two would make such a cute couple.\"","\"I never-\" Vannir noticed the hilarity in the room and knew that his outrage would only fuel it further. \"Fine. Haug’s rejecting me broke my heart. Happy now?\"","His voice oozed sarcasm, but no one seemed to notice.","\"He admitted it!\" Akkhar played the Rememberer of the events. \"Quick! Let’s show it to the others!\"","\"Not if I kill you first!\" Vannir demonstrated the reflexes of a cheetah and caught Akkhar before he could take a single step.","\"What’s this noise?\" Ryla asked as pans and pots fell to the ground with loud clangs.","\"My kids are roughhousing as usual.\" Haug replied, waving goodbye to Garrik.","He and Fluffy ran to the playground for their magical games with the Fastarrows and the Verhens.","\"Now that we are alone, I want to thank you from the bottom of my heart, Haug.\" Ryla gave him a deep bow that instantly quieted the kitchens. \"I know this is just a job for you, but you didn’t have to be so kind to Garrik, let alone so patient.\"","Dryna and the others had stopped squabbling and eavesdropped on the conversation in the other room with every spell and bloodline ability they had.","\"Most people would have gotten annoyed with my son, and only someone with a heart of Davross would have taken so much time of their day to prepare a single serving of such complicated dishes.","\"I’ll be forever grateful to Lith for bringing you here, and even more to you and your staff for making my son’s life much more magical.\"","\"Please, don’t thank me.\" Haug replied with a sadness that worried Ryla and wounded her heart. \"I don’t deserve your praise. I’m not the good man you think. I like Garrik, and I love my job, but I also had an ulterior motive.\"","Ryla stiffened as the many strange things she had noticed fell into place. There could only be one possible explanation for Haug’s sweet attentions, his heartwarming kindness, and tender gazes.","\"You’re after Garrik!\" She said, her eyes blazing with elemental power. \"You want the power of his bloodline.\"","’Haug is an Awakened human mage, and Garrik is the first stable full-blooded evolved human.’ She thought. ’Haug must have gotten close to my son because he wants to experiment on Garrik or at least examine him to discover the secret of human evolution!’","\"I wish I were just a scumbag.\" Haug ignored the threat she posed and sighed melancholically. \"If I were, we wouldn’t have this conversation, and I could avoid facing you.\"","Ryla’s eyes and wings released the power of the elements as confusion replaced her rage.","’He’s right, and I’m an idiot. Why would he share his plans with me if he had bad intentions towards my son?’ She pondered.","\"I’m not after Garrik. I don’t care about the secret of human evolution.\" Haug cleared his throat in embarrassment. \"I’m interested in his mother.\"","Ryla’s cheeks flushed, her mind understanding what the bartender was saying but refusing to believe it until she heard it loud and clear.","\"I’m interested in you.\" Haug continued. \"What I’m trying to say is, I like you, Ryla.\"","\"Me?\" She asked in disbelief, her blue skin turning pinker and her wings fluttering with short, rapid movements.","’If those things work anything like a bird’s, at least she’s not offended, nor does she want to get out of here.’ Haug inwardly sighed in relief. ’She should be excited, and this is a good sign.’","\"Yes, and I’d like to ask you out.\" He nodded. \"To get to know each other outside of our client-caterer relationship.\"","\"You mean... like a date?\" Ryla’s face turned to a bright shade of pink, and her wings flapped in a frenzy."]},{"number":4502,"title":"Chapter 4502 Chaotic Mess (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Not like a date. A date.\" Haug clarified.","\"Yes! I’d love to!\" Ryla smiled from the bottom of her heart, and her wings flapped so hard she now floated a few centimeters off the ground.","Haug should have been on cloud nine, yet he shared but a fraction of her excitement.","’Don’t delude yourself, old man. This doesn’t mean she likes you. Only that she likes the idea of having her first date.’ He thought. ’There’s no way to know if she wouldn’t react the same way even if anyone else asked her out.’","\"We... I mean, I might have a problem, though.\" Her wings stopped moving, and her expression tensed. \"I... I’m...\"","\"Don’t worry, Morok told me everything already.\" Haug noticed her distress and did his best to reassure her.","\"He did?\" Ryla went pale, and her wings froze in a half-unfurled stance, ready to take flight at a moment’s notice.","’I’m going to kill him!’ She thought.","\"Yes.\" Haug replied. \"He told me of your fallen state and that stepping out of the mana geyser would shorten your lifespan. You don’t have to worry about that. I’ll take care of Warping us across mana geysers until we reach our destination.\"","\"Oh, that!\" She sighed in relief, and her smile returned.","’I was actually worried about turning into a monster and Morok telling Haug about the circumstances of my... relationship with Glemos. Thank the gods he didn’t.’ She thought, and she was dead wrong.","\"Also, if it makes you feel more comfortable, we could bring Garrik with us.\" Haug said. \"I want to get to know you and-\"","\"No!\" Ryla cut him short, her cheeks flushed and her fists clenched. \"I mean, that’s not necessary. I’m comfortable around you, Haug, and...\"","She struggled to let the words out and needed to take deep breaths to find the strength to say what she wanted.","\"And I’d like to get to know you as Haug the man instead of Haug the bartender, just like I want you to get to know me as Ryla instead of Garrik’s mother.\"","\"I would love to.\" He smiled back at her, and for the first time since the start of that conversation, he meant it. \"What about Garrik? Won’t he feel lonely?\"","\"It’s just one evening.\" She shrugged. \"Besides, I’m not leaving him stranded in the Blood Desert, but surrounded by his family. Give me a second.\"","She rushed outside, found Morok, and carried him over her head inside the Tavern.","\"Haug here asked me out, and I said yes.\" She said, half-proud and half-embarrassed. \"Can you look after Garrik for me during our date?\"","\"With pleasure.\" The Tyrant nodded, exchanging a quick look with the bartender. \"My children love their uncle, and we’ll protect him against anything and anyone. Isn’t that right, kids?\"","Orikan and Jirya had followed their father with their tiny wings and were now clinging to his shoulders with their claws. They answered his question by opening their mouths and showing a row of shark-like teeth that spun at high speed like a circular buzzsaw.","\"I didn’t know Tyrants could do that.\" Haug said in shock.","\"Me neither.\" Morok scratched his chin. \"Guys, we have a problem.\"","\"Wah?\" The twins looked at their father, waiting to be praised.","\"Don’t you do that again unless it’s absolutely necessary. Especially around your mother when she’s about to breastfeed you, or you’ll give her a heart attack. Okay?\" He asked, and the children nodded. \"Good kids. Now let’s go. I need to find a way to break the news to Quylla.\"","\"Why do you need to tell her about my date?\" Ryla blushed.","\"I was talking about the teeth thing.\" The Tyrant replied.","\"Oh. Sorry about that.\" She cleared her throat in embarrassment.","\"Don’t worry, Ryla. Just have fun.\"","***","Lith waited until the Travelling Tavern left the Verhen Mansion before resuming his experiments with Dread Magic, Void Magic, and his newfound bloodline abilities.","’Whatever that emerald thing was, I can’t trigger it at will.’ He filled his eyes and wings with the power of all elements, yet he could only activate one Indech bloodline ability at a time.","’Maybe it’s because your mana organs are still partially atrophied.’ Solus was in her Vritra form, trying to understand if she had any special abilities and how to control them. ’Back then, your energy wings split up.","’You are an Awakened Indech, after all, yet you still don’t look like one.’","’Point taken.’ He inwardly sighed. ’What about you? How is your Indech training going?’","’I’ve mastered the theory behind our powers for weeks. Too bad that putting it into practice is not that easy.’ Solus switched to her Indech form, but even with the tower and the Hands of Menadion, her Swirling Wind was mediocre at best.","She needed her full focus just to draw in and stir the world energy. Splitting it into its elemental components was beyond her.","’Don’t give up. There is no shortcut. You need to keep at it until your human mana organs learn how to crawl before they can walk and then run.’ Lith said to encourage her. ’It took me months to get here.’","’I know, but it’s much worse for me.’ Solus whined. ’Look at this!’","She turned into her Talos form, taking the appearance of a short, golden construct with mana crystals studded into her surface and a blazing fire for hair.","’I have no idea what I can do in this form. I’ve trained for weeks now, and I’m still at square one. Same for this!’","She shapeshifted into her Dragon Form, her body covered in pristine white scales and her membranous wings covered in prismatic crystal feathers.","’I don’t even have a name for this form, and I don’t know the first thing about it.’ She exhaled sharply. ’I have so much work ahead of me that it makes me want to cry!’","’My advice is to focus on one thing at a time.’ Lith replied. ’The Indech is your best bet since we already know most of its abilities. Use it to build up your confidence, but practice the other forms from time to time. Unused muscles can’t develop.’","’I know.’ Solus Warped to the Greenhouse for a moment.","She stared at the Camellia Valeron had created for Kamila to fuel her competitive spirit before returning to the Firing Range to resume her training.","’What about you?’ She asked. ’What’s your next goal?’","’I too have a lot on my plate, but I’m trying to work together with my Sigil Demons and Golems to replicate what I managed to do in Verendi under the effects of the Eldritch resonance.’","Lith pointed at his five Demons, each at the seven eyes level, and the two Golems. Black chains linked the Demons to Lith and each other, while Spirit tendrils connected them to the constructs.","They were working together to establish battle formations and specific combinations of spells they would have to impart to feral Demons of the Darkness once they answered Lith’s call.","’I learned a long while ago that I can use my Demons as focus points for my arrays and to form runes for my spells, but even after reaching the bright violet, it’s still too much for me alone.’"]},{"number":4503,"title":"Chapter 4503 Poison in the Family (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’Once the fight begins, I can’t deliver precise instructions to dozens of Demons without losing focus on my own battle. There is no point in having a killer magical formation if my enemy can just get close and kill me without me even noticing.’","’Sounds hard.’ Solus noticed the grimaces of the Demons as they tried to coordinate their efforts and the actions of a hundred practice constructs the tower had conjured for them.","’And it’s even harder than it looks.’ Lith replied.","The training continued until lunchtime. Lith and Solus took breaks only when Raldarak needed a fresh diaper or Valeron and Elysia asked to see them.","The kids were happy and surrounded by their friends and relatives, but they didn’t like being separated from their parents for too long.","\"Hi, Ral.\" Trion took the baby boy in his arms and rocked him gently. \"Do you remember me?\"","\"Mama.\" The baby boy replied.","\"Close enough.\" The Sigil Demons chuckled. \"I’m your uncle, Trion, but I’m okay with Dio or Tio. Anything that even closely resembles my name will do.\"","\"Mama.\" Ral nodded with a serious expression on his small face.","\"Get in line, lil bro.\" Rena snorted. \"With Elysia as his third word, I deserve to be the fourth, since no one in this family thinks about me.\"","She pouted and glared at Lith.","\"I hope to be next.\" Valeron the Second lowered his gaze, feeling guilty for the tension that his flower had created in the family.","\"Me too!\" Rena realized her blunder and froze. \"I’m sorry, Val. I’m not angry at you.\"","\"Don’t worry, Auntie.\" Valeron said, yet his voice lacked conviction.","\"I noticed you’ve taken your duties as an uncle more seriously, Trion.\" Lith rushed to change the topic to spare his son’s feelings.","\"Yes, Lith.\" Trion didn’t miss how his little brother still called him strictly by name and didn’t care about his feelings. \"I’m just happy to have the chance to spend time with my siblings, nieces, and nephew after the mess I’ve made of my life.","\"I know I’ve not been much of a brother to you and Tista. I can’t make it up to you two, but I can try to be better for Aran, Surin, and your children.\"","\"About that.\" Elina turned to look at Tista. \"Any news on that front?\"","\"Mom!\" Tista almost choked on her bacon. \"Not in front of the kids.\"","\"Why?\" Elina raised an eyebrow. \"Why shouldn’t they know if Bodya has finally proposed and you’re about to marry?\"","\"He didn’t, and I’m not.\" She dismissed the argument with a sweep of her hand. \"Case closed.\"","\"Do you mind if I give the kids a few flight lessons?\" Trion asked. \"They can use the fresh air and I some bonding time.\"","\"Be my guest.\" Lith shrugged. \"Take Trouble as your body and don’t leave the Mansion’s premises, though. Safety first.\"","He turned to look at Valeron the Second. Only the Griffon bloodline had offered the baby boy protection, and there were still plenty of people, Awakened and not, who wanted to hurt him because of what his mother had done.","’We can’t rely on the Dragons.’ Lith said via the black chains. ’Their promise to avenge Valeron is a deterrent only against those who want to kill him, but it’s irrelevant to those who want to kidnap or hurt him.’","’Don’t worry. I won’t let you down again.’ Trion replied. ’Scratch that. I won’t let the kids down. No matter the cost.’","Aran and Leria had heard enough about Trion to have a poor impression of him, and even after getting to know him, their relationship hadn’t improved much. He’d been absent for most of their lives, and the few times their parents had mentioned him, it wasn’t to say good things.","The triples were young enough to be more open and forgiving, but they saw Leria’s weariness around him and trusted their big sister’s judgment. Raldarak, Elysia, Valeron, and Surin, however, were different.","They trusted Trion unconditionally, offering him a clean slate upon which to build their relationship. He was loving and caring with them, afraid of repeating his past mistakes.","’ Orpal was a monster as a kid already, but I was dumber than a brick.’ He inwardly grimaced. ’Gods, I had a family most people can only dream about, and I threw it away out of blind pride.’","\"What do you say, kids? Would you like to fly around the park with Uncle Trion?\" He actually said, smiling at the babies.","Raldarak squeaked with joy, while Elysia nodded enthusiastically.","\"I’d love to, Uncle.\" Valeron looked at Lith, and waited for him to nod before answering.","After the meal ended, Trion brought the kids to the park and let them fly in front of him, following them closely. He carried Surin strapped to an enchanted baby carrier on his chest, giving her the thrill of flight and the safety of a multi-layered barrier.","\"Do you have to do that, sweetie?\" Elina asked.","\"Do what, Mom?\" Lith asked as he changed the settings of the tower’s defense system to monitor the children closely.","He set Valeron and Surin as top priority since they had no Guardian watching over them.","\"Be so cold with your brother.\" Elina replied. \"Your children can feel it. Or at least, Valeron can.\"","\"I-\" Lith wanted to argue that Aran was his only brother, but he didn’t want to hurt his mother with such cruel words. \"I’m trying, but it’s not easy. Trion had years to show through his actions who he was, and I believe him.","\"Words are cheap, Mom. All the apologies in the world change nothing. I can feel Trion’s sincerity through the black chains, but it doesn’t mean much. He didn’t change his mind until it was literally too late.","\"He needed to die to understand what kind of... man he had become. That’s hardly an achievement. Most people would just carry their last-second regret to the afterlife. He’s just...\"","\"Lucky.\" Elina felt his hesitation and completed the phrase for him. \"I know. Though, we are also lucky to have him, or at least I am. I got a second chance with my wayward son. I got to know I was right about him.","\"That Trion never hated us nor was he a bad person. He was just lost. How and when we found him doesn’t matter, sweetie. Every second we spend together is a gift.\" She paused to look Lith in the eyes until his stern gaze softened.","\"I’m not asking you to forgive your brother. Your relationship is between the two of you. I’m asking, begging you to be nicer to him, baby. Maybe you don’t notice it, but even your silent reproach weighs heavily on Trion’s head.","\"Aran, Leria, and everyone who looks at you as their role model mirrors your behavior towards him. We don’t know how much time your brother has left with us. Please, don’t poison them against him.\"","\"I’m sorry, Mom.\" Lith replied. \"It wasn’t my intention. I’ll cut him some slack.\"","\"It’s all I ask.\" She gave him a peck on the cheek. \"Thank you. You truly are my miracle baby. You’ve given me my two lost sons back.\"","The love coating his mother’s words made Lith feel terrible about himself."]},{"number":4504,"title":"Chapter 4504 Poison in the Family (Part 2)","paragraphs":["’Mom is aware I might not be her true son, yet she doesn’t care.’ He clenched his teeth. ’Her behavior towards me hasn’t changed one bit after she learned I’m part Abomination. Her love is as unwavering as my spite.","’Even after Trion did everything I asked, even after my black chains confirmed that his change of heart is not a façade, I can barely bring myself to tolerate him. Mom is right. Trion’s days with us are numbered.","’He promised to stay until Meln is dead, but that means nothing. The moment his rage fades, or his attachment to our family falters, his connection with my black chains will break, and his soul will move on.","’Kami suggested that I help my Demons make new good memories if I want to keep them by my side, yet I keep treating Trion like dirt. Maybe it’s too late for us. Maybe we’ll never be close brothers, but we can be civil.","’He was scum to me, but he can be a good uncle for my children and a positive influence for Rena’s. The grudge between us can’t poison our little ones. Not anymore.’","Lith took a deep breath and did one of the hardest things in the world for him. He let go of his shared past with Trion.","He didn’t forgive or forget what his older brother had done or how he had treated their parents. Those things would never go away, but now they didn’t influence Lith’s behavior or how he treated Trion unless he made them relevant again.","’This is your second chance with me, big brother.’ Lith said via the black chains, and the surprise almost sent Trion spinning in midair. ’Be careful. There won’t be a third.’","***","Lith invited Baba Yaga over in the afternoon to practice tier four Dread Magic together. There was still a long way to go before mixing a normal and a Cursed Element, but the closer they got to success, the more Lith itched to apply Void Magic to Dread Magic.","\"What is Solus doing, if you don’t mind me asking?\" The Mother had to take a short break from her practice to let her charred arms regenerate.","\"Practicing with her other forms.\" Lith replied as he failed to weave the earth and the Cinder element together.","His attempt to create a half-Dread version of Raging Sun resulted in a mass of burnt soil that exploded in his face with annoying consequences.","\"She’s focusing on the Indech, moving on to experimenting on the other two when she gets sick of Swirling Wind.\"","\"Establishing solid foundations is as important as it’s mind-numbing.\" Baba Yaga thought about her Dread Magic exercises and how boring their practice was. \"What about Zoreth? It’s been a while since you gave me any news about her.\"","\"I don’t know.\" Lith shrugged. \"I haven’t heard from her in a while ei-\"","A sudden pull at his consciousness drew him to his Council amulet. Before answering, he performed a head count with the Watchtower and checked everyone’s position.","\"This is the first time you’ve ever called me, Lotho.\" Lith said as the hologram of the Plant Representative towered over him. \"This must be important, or you’d have sent Raagu ahead.\"","\"It’s very important.\" The Treant looked like a massive oak tree that had somehow developed thick legs and arms that could easily crush a bull like a fly. \"This is a very delicate matter, and it requires the utmost discretion.","\"I know we don’t like or trust each other much, Verhen, but I can’t afford anyone learning about this conversation. Are you alone?\"","\"Yes.\" Lith lied through his teeth, leaving the Mother where she was and Warping Solus by her side. \"I’m in one of my secret labs. Now, tell me what this is about.\"","\"I...\" Lotho’s amber eyes looked around like a trapped animal searching for a way out. \"Gods, this is so embarrassing that I don’t know how to say it.\"","Plant folks and Fae had barely any morality and could easily be classified as sociopaths according to human standards. Seeing an ancient Fae like Lotho so flustered was beyond unsettling.","’This guy would be able to tell me about how he ate his brother alive while inviting me to discuss business over dinner. Calling whatever this is, delicate, is an understatement.’ Lith thought.","\"Are you in love with my sister, Tista?\" He asked, trying to guess the source of Lotho’s distress.","\"No!\" The quick and disgusted reply brooked no further argument. \"Yet with your stupid human reasoning you’ve gotten very close to the truth. This is about your family, but not in the way you think.\"","\"Then you better speak clearly and quickly, or I’ll interpret your words as a threat and deal with you accordingly.\" Lith snarled.","\"Great Mother Almighty, I’m sorry. I’m so out of my mind that I didn’t realize how weird I made it sound.\" Lotho’s apology sent a cold shiver down Lith’s spine.","Powerful creatures rarely apologized, and Fae never did.","\"I’m not threatening you. I called you to ask for your help on behalf of a member of my clan. A female member of my clan.\" Lotho said, pausing for a long, awkward moment before adding. \"A stupid, arrogant Fae who sided with Meln.\"","\"What did you say?\" Lith’s voice lowered to a whisper, but it was as cold as ice and as sharp as steel.","\"I won’t even try to excuse her actions, but please, listen to me until the end.\" Lotho said, and Lith nodded for him to continue. \"This Fae temporarily joined the Dead King’s side, but not as you might think.","\"She didn’t take his blood, didn’t take part in any of his crazy plans, nor was she aware of any of them. She did what I assume many Fae have tried to do to you. Get inside your bed to receive the power of your bloodline straight from the source.\"","\"She slept with him?\" Lith was flabbergasted.","\"Yes, her plan was quite ingenious.\" Lotho nodded. \"She pretended to give a damn about him and got pregnant with his child. She knew that to become an Upyr, she would have needed regular injections of Meln’s blood and assumed that the baby’s blood would work just the same.","\"She was right. As soon as she confirmed the pregnancy, she escaped the Dead King’s fortress at the first opportunity. She returned to her family offering her newfound powers and the might of a Divine Beast in exchange for their forgiveness.\"","\"Are you talking about her or her baby?\" Lith asked. \"Also, did they take her back?\"","\"I’m talking about both.\" Lotho replied. \"And of course, her clan took her back. She was now a powerful hybrid, and her son was supposed to grow into a Vurdalak. With all the bloodline abilities of his deranged father and none of his madness, the boy gave any member of the clan the chance to become a Divine Beast if they so desired.","\"I know that you consider us Fae heartless monsters, but I doubt many clans would have turned down such an offer, no matter the woman’s race of origin.\"","\"Sadly, I agree.\" Lith nodded. \"Why didn’t you tell me about her sooner, and why are you talking in the past tense?\""]},{"number":4505,"title":"Chapter 4505 Humiliating Secret (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"I didn’t tell you about her because I didn’t know about what she had done either.\" Lotho sighed. \"Nobody outside her direct bloodline knew. For what it’s worth, I already had her tell me everything she knew about the Dead King, and it was worth nothing.","\"She left when Meln moved out of his hideout and has no idea where he went. Even if she shared her intel the moment she came back to Garlen, it would have already been too late.","\"As for your second question, the answer is the reason for my call. There is something wrong with this Fae and her child. Something terribly wrong that not even the regenerative powers of my race can fix.","\"Her clan members asked for my help because they had no other choice, and I’m calling you for the same reason. I’ve already visited the Fae. I used every spell and bloodline ability at my disposal, yet nothing worked.","\"I even called some of the best Healers among my kind, Fae whose greed and reputation I could trust. The prognosis is always the same. Kill the child and save the mother.","\"No one wants to do that, though, especially the pregnant Fae. So, here I am, Lith Verhen, asking for your help. What do you say?\"","\"That I have questions.\" The hatred Lith felt for his disowned brother and his offspring didn’t cloud his mind one bit. \"What do you mean, whose greed you can trust? And why didn’t you just kill them both if you deem them a threat?","\"I know you Fae only believe in the law of the jungle, and going to such lengths to help a member of your bloodline who already betrayed your trust it’s not like you. I want the full story, Lotho, or I’m ending this call.\"","The Treant’s amber eyes narrowed in annoyance for a heartbeat before they relaxed to a neutral expression. Fae were pragmatic creatures. Lotho knew to be cornered and that anger would solve nothing.","Rather than wasting time he didn’t have, he dropped the mask.","\"You’re right, Verhen. Under any other circumstance, her bloodline would have already put her down without a second thought. She was pardoned under the condition that she would grant her family access to the power of a Divine Beast, and the deal is most likely off.","\"Without it, no Fae bloodline would show her any mercy. Yet this is different. We have no idea what has gone wrong with the woman and her child. Maybe it’s the Dead King’s accursed bloodline’s fault, or maybe we are the problem.","\"Maybe we Fae are a dead evolutionary branch and unsuitable to wield the power of a Divine Beast. If this second scenario turns out to be true, it would mean there’s no hope for us.","\"That even if one of my kind became a Guardian, Fae wouldn’t be able to become a Divine Plant, a Blossomed Being, or whatever the offspring of the plant Guardian would be called.","\"We’d have to start over from our plant folk brethren and try to understand what’s gone wrong with Fae and in what new direction we need to move. This is why we have yet to kill mother and baby.","\"Also, it’s the reason I needed greedy, reliable Fae. I offered them the power of the Vurdalak in exchange for their silence and help, and they accepted. Alas, they didn’t fare any better than me.","\"No progress has been made, and our understanding of the illness is nil. This is the full story, Verhen. I’m holding nothing back. I swear it upon my Root.\"","It was a plant folk’s most sacred vow, so Lith was inclined to believe the Treant, but that was it.","\"What about my reward?\" Lith asked. \"Assuming I can do something about this, you Fae are the only ones that benefit from my success.\"","\"Don’t be coy with me, Verhen!\" Lotho snarled. \"Your reward is the unique opportunity to study your hated brother’s bloodline. The baby is still a Vurdalak, and there’s no telling how much you can learn from him.","\"He’d be a willing patient, and you’d have all the time you need to use any diagnostic equipment at your disposal. If you agree to help us, you get to study both an Upyr and a Vurdalak, Verhen.","\"You can learn first-hand what makes them tick and look for any weak point that might help you in killing Meln and disposing of his forces. Moreover, even if you can’t help us or deliver us the worst news possible, that knowledge would still stay with you.","\"We Fae might lose the woman, the child, and discover we are a fallen race, but you would get your prize and our humiliating secret with you. I’d say this is more than enough payment. Take it or leave it.\"","’He’s right. This is an incredible bargain for me.’ Lith’s expression betrayed none of his thoughts, his face fixed in a stone mask. ’Yet just because I can do it, it doesn’t mean that I should.","’The best line of action for me is to go there, learn everything I can about Meln and his Divine Beast thralls, and claim there’s nothing I can do about it. The idea of helping someone who sided with him, even out of pure convenience, and his child makes me want to puke.’","’How can you say that, Lith?’ Solus echoed in his mind. ’I can understand your spite for Meln. You know I hate him just as much as you. I can also understand your unwillingness to help the Fae. Yet the child is innocent.","’He didn’t choose the circumstances under which he was conceived nor his parents. Can you really turn your back on him like that?’","Lith mulled over the question long enough to have many telepathic conversations with her.","’Darn, this was the wrong day to decide to let go of the past and give people a chance.’ He inwardly sighed.","\"I’m willing to give you a hand, Lotho.\" Lith said, and his sincerity made Solus proud. \"Though I have one condition.\"","\"Name it.\" The Treant sighed, hoping it wouldn’t be anything too outrageous.","\"I’m not coming alone.\" Lith replied. \"I don’t trust you or the Fae not to kill me to keep your shameful secret, especially if I succeed in saving the baby. My existence would become a problem for your kind, and in their home, I’d be easy prey.\"","\"I can’t argue with that.\" Lotho nodded. \"Getting rid of you as soon as you’ve outlived your usefulness is exactly what a Fae bloodline would do. The little Vurdalak would make your Tiamat bloodline redundant to us.\"","\"I know.\" Lith said. \"Hence, I’m bringing one more person with me, and I’m telling everyone I trust where I’m going. This is not up for debate. Refuse my condition and our deal is off.\"","\"Right now, I’m so desperate I wouldn’t say no even if you brought along an entire army.\" Lotho’s sincerity was a pleasant surprise. \"To prove my good faith, I’m giving you the coordinates of the Fae’s secret hideout.","\"You can reach it with your means and at your convenience, so you can verify it’s not a trap. I’m already there. Call me when you arrive, and I’ll come to you. Lotho out.\""]},{"number":4506,"title":"Chapter 4506 Humiliating Secret (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"You are the one I want as my plus one, Yaga.\" Lith said after storing away his dimensional amulet. \"Please, I need your help.\"","\"No need to be polite. Of course, I’ll help you.\" The Mother replied. \"This is a great opportunity for me to study the workings of my deranged daughter. If you didn’t ask me to accompany you, I’d have begged you to let me come with you.","\"What I don’t understand is why you thought of me in the first place.\"","\"It’s not that hard.\" Lith shrugged. \"You are one of the greatest experts on life forces on Mogar and Night’s mother. If someone can understand what she’s done to Meln, that’s you.","\"Also, you are a white core, and everybody knows about your tower. Your presence will deter the Fae from trying anything funny and provide me the cover I need to use the Ears and Eyes of Menadion.","\"Everything we learn from the artifacts, we can claim it’s thanks to your powers or tower. Without you, the Fae might suspect something or think that my bloodline is more powerful than it is.","\"My family is already under siege, and I don’t want the entire Fae race to become obsessed with them.\"","\"All excellent points.\" Baba Yaga nodded. \"When do we move?\"","\"Now.\" Lith replied. \"The situation is critical, and the Fae already wasted a lot of time before calling me. There is not a second to lose.\"","He Warped Kamila to the tower, explaining everything to her via a mind link.","’Please, find a nice cover story and don’t tell Mom about the child.’ Lith said. ’She hates Meln like everyone else, but that boy is innocent and her grandchild. I don’t want her to grieve him if I fail to save him.’","’Can’t we talk about this?’ Kamila asked. ’I’m the one who has to lie to our family.’","’Sadly, there is no time. Wish me luck.’ Lith Blinked her in the keep and charged up the Tower Warp.","’Kick his ass.’ Kamila replied. ’This is no illness. It’s just Meln, and I know you won’t let him win.’","Starforge moved to the nearest mana geyser to the Fae secret hideout Lith knew, and from there they moved with Bloodhaven.","\"We really need to travel more and mark more geysers.\" Solus sighed. \"If not for Malyshka, this would take a while.\"","\"We’ll stop on the mana geysers we meet on the way to let you imprint them.\" Baba Yaga said. \"Now let’s focus. Lith, give me Solus’ ring. You don’t want the magical formations of the Fae to detect something that powerful on your finger.\"","\"Way ahead of you.\" Lith handed her what looked like a stone pendant of a dragon coiled around a precious gem.","\"Great minds do think alike.\" She shapeshifted into her Crone form and put the pendant at her neck.","The group reached their destination in a few minutes. It was a thick woods in the east side of the Kingdom, the like they had seen hundred others. If not for the presence of a powerful mana geyser, the place would have been unremarkable.","\"My tower can siphon the world energy even from here. What about yours, Solus?\" The Crone asked.","\"The Fae’s magical formations take most of the mana geyser’s output, but I should be able to nibble a bit of world energy without them noticing if I take things nice and easy.\" Solus replied. \"Marking it is impossible, though.\"","\"Do what you can; I’m calling Lotho.\" Lith said.","The Treant emerged from a sycamore smaller than him that stretched like rubber upon his passage.","\"Good gods!\" He said when he recognized Bloodhaven.","Baba Yaga had kept her tower outside the area of effect of the detection arrays, and her cloaking enchantments made Bloodhaven invisible to anything but regular sight.","\"Stop gawking at a lady. It’s rude.\" Lith walked towards the entrance with the Crone one step behind him.","\"You know the Red Mother? How?\" Countless thoughts ran through Lotho’s mind, and not one was peaceful.","\"Know is a big word.\" The Crone replied. \"We just have something in common. Or rather, someone. I want Night dead, and he wants Meln dead. It would have been stupid of me not to give Verhen the means to contact me. Now make way, little sprout.\"","\"You are a white core, and that’s your mage tower.\" Lotho retorted. \"My friends will feel threatened by your presence.\"","\"What a coincidence, I feel threatened by them.\" Lith sneered. \"I won’t go anywhere without her.\"","\"Fine!\" Lotho raised his hands in surrender and gestured for them to follow him into the array field.","\"Why aren’t we using that entrance?\" Lith pointed at the sycamore.","\"That’s me putting your safety first.\" The Treant replied. \"Instead of forcing you to walk underground in a fortress you consider unfriendly, we’ll move above ground until we reach our destination.","\"I’m giving you an escape route at all times and keeping the Fae from surrounding you in a location where they have the field advantage.\"","\"How nice of you.\" Lith said.","’My bet is the Fae don’t want you to study their facility and magical formations.’ Solus said. ’They are protecting themselves under the guise of protecting you.’","’As Yaga said, great minds.’ Lith inwardly nodded.","\"Here we are.\" The walk through the woods was as brief as it was uneventful.","Aside from a few birds and critters, the Eyes of Menadion hadn’t spotted anything or anyone.","\"Do you want me to go first or last?\" Lotho placed his hands on an oak tree, and its bark opened like a door, revealing a long, luxurious corridor leading downstairs.","\"You first, then me, then Lady Yaga.\" Lith replied. \"You’ll be my wooden shield, and she’ll keep our escape route open at all times.\"","Lotho furrowed the bark of his face, but didn’t comment. The inside of the oak tree turned out to have been stretched with dimensional magic, and there was enough space for two Treants to walk abreast.","The stairs led to a single door that opened on what Lith recognized as a medical ward. The environment was sterile and filled with medical and diagnostic arrays. The only furniture was a bed for the patient and a bedstand.","The walls and floor were made of wood, so any Fae visitor could conjure a chair or anything they needed the moment they needed it.","The patient turned out to be a Dryad of rare beauty, with hair the flaming red of autumn leaves and eyes as blue as diamonds. Her swollen belly drew Lith’s attention, but not as much as two different dirty-white flames burning with a sickening light.","One orbited over the mother’s head, and the other marked the unborn child’s position.","\"Order and Chaos, what’s wrong with her?\" Baba Yaga asked.","The Dryad’s lovely features were twisted in a rictus of focus and pain. She gritted her teeth and clenched the bed’s wooden headboard as if her life depended on it. She was covered in sweat-like sap that drenched her clothes and stained the bedsheets.","\"I don’t want to eat my child, that’s what!\" She snarled in fury, her eyes burning with violet mana. \"I don’t want to, but I have to. I-\""]},{"number":4507,"title":"Chapter 4507 Not a Hybrid (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Fury replaced pain when she focused long enough on the newcomers to recognize Lith.","\"Leech!\" A red flame appeared over her head, and the Dryad breathed a burst of Fire Soul at him.","The ward’s arrays dispelled the corrupted fire and restricted the Dryad’s movements. Her body writhed and spasmed in anger, her features shapeshifting from Dryad to Upyr nonstop for a while, before she stopped struggling.","\"Leech.\" Her voice was a whisper coated in poison.","\"Long story short, this is Althika, and she was fine until the day the Dead King attacked the Undead Court branch of Bornar. Then, that silver flame appeared over mother and child.","\"At first, everyone rejoiced, thinking Althika had discovered a new bloodline ability thanks to her unborn baby. Yet less than a day later, something went terribly wrong. She was experimenting with her new powers when a patch of her body mutated.","\"We don’t know why, how, or even what that patch is, only that since that happened, Althika hasn’t been herself anymore. She claims-\"","\"That this is no power.\" She pointed at the flames above her head, cutting Lotho short. \"This is a curse. I was a normal bright cyan-cored Dryad before I joined the Dead King’s side.","\"Yet after getting pregnant with his child and reaching the blue core, I didn’t evolve into a Titania. No matter how much I practiced Accumulation or the baby helped me refine my core, even after reaching the deep violet, I’m still a Dryad.","\"It unsettled me, but I could live with it since my Upyr side makes me a Divine Beast. Since the silver flames appeared, however, I’m always hungry, and nothing I eat puts a dent in it. It’s consuming me, driving me crazy.","\"It doesn’t crave meat or nutrients from the soil. It wants me to consume my own child. To feed on his life force and add it to my own. And you know what the worst part is?\" Althika teared up, her fury turning into despair.","\"I feel deep in my gut that the silver flames are supposed to start a battle to determine who’s stronger and deserves to live. Yet my child is going to let me win because he trusts me! Please, kill me if you have to, but save my baby!\"","Those words confirmed Baba Yaga’s darkest theories about the origins of the Vurdalak race. She had discarded them because there was no evidence to support them, but now the evidence lay right before her, crying.","\"Don’t fret, child. It’s too soon to lose hope.\" The Crone didn’t let her worries transpire and smiled warmly at the Dryad to reassure her. \"I need to examine you to assess your condition. It’s okay if I use my breathing technique on you?\"","\"Yes.\" Althika sobbed. \"I recognize you, Red Mother, and I don’t care about what happens to me. Don’t ask my permission. Do anything you can to save my child.\"","\"I will, but before that, I need to meet my host.\" She turned to Lotho. \"Who’s the idiot who rules over this bloodline? I want to look them in their face as I give them a piece of my mind.\"","\"I’d like to keep that confidential.\" Lotho scratched the foliage covering his head.","\"And I’d like to start treating this poor girl as soon as possible.\" The Crone replied. \"How can I trust someone to uphold their word if they don’t even have the guts to step into the light?\"","\"You make a compelling argument, Lady Yaga.\" A wooden wall opened, and a stunning Titania walked into the room. \"Nice to meet you. I’m Naphila, matriarch of House Redleaf.\"","She was over 3 meters (10 feet) tall, with wheat-blond hair, light green eyes, and slightly long, pointy ears. She wore a sleeveless dress made of vines that covered everything under her collarbone, leaving only her rosy face and hands exposed.","Thin branches and leaves that were part of her own body formed what looked like a circlet around her head. Her slender fingers ended in long nails that, with the wood’s wrinkled appearance and darker color, made them look like they belonged to a much older woman.","He beauty surpassed that of all Dryads Lith had ever met, yet he sensed no kindness or warmth in her. Every fiber of his being warned him that the creature before him was a predator as ruthless as an Abomination.","\"I’m sorry for this pathetic display of weakness you had to endure. Dryads are usually calm and composed, but mixing our blood with other species can lead to unfortunate side effects.\"","\"Before you ask, Lady Naphila considers Althika’s love for her unborn child a weakness, Lith.\" The Crone said with all the spite her voice could convey. \"Also, yes, she’s the real matriarch of this household.","\"I know it because she bears the same energy signature as the arrays in the room. I’m glad you’re such a piece of work, Lady Naphila. It makes my work much easier.\" A wave of Baba Yaga’s hand brought the Titania to her knees and ripped the Root out of her chest.","\"Make one wrong move, order one of your elders to so much as say something I don’t like, and I’ll squash you like the bug you think Althika is. Are we clear?\"","\"Yes.\" The Titania gasped, ordering her cloaked allies in the adjacent rooms to call off the attack on Baba Yaga with a hidden sign.","Naphila craved the power of the Vurdalak, but since it had already proven problematic, she considered the secret of the white core a much greater boon for the Redleaf clan.","\"Good.\" The Crone nodded. \"I’m willing to bet purified Davross that if Lith came here alone and failed to cure Althika, you’d have employed whatever you wanted to use against me to strap him to the bed and make a few more Divine Beasts the old-fashioned way. Do you deny it?\"","\"No.\" Naphila shook her head.","\"What?\" Lotho roared in outrage. \"You gave me your word, Naphila! I gave Verhen mine!\"","\"Stupid fossil.\" She snarled through gritted teeth. \"Who cares about honor when presented with the opportunity for true power? If I can’t have the Vurdalak bloodline, the Tiamat will have to do.","\"As for your precious honor, once I killed you and Verhen, nobody would’ve known what happened here, and the Council would have only you to blame for Verhen’s disappearance.\"","\"I swear I didn’t know about this, Verhen. I would have never brought you here if I suspected Naphila’s intentions.\" Lotho said.","\"This only makes it worse, Lotho, because I expected something like this to happen since you called me.\" Lith snorted. \"Why do you think I brought Lady Yaga along?\"","The plant representative gave him a deep bow and lowered his head in shame.","After ordering Naphila to use the arrays to restrain anyone powerful enough to disturb her work, Baba Yaga moved to the bedside. She used her breathing technique, Sun and Moon, to examine Althika and her child.","The Crone also used the Ears and the Eyes of Menadion, sharing part of the burden with Lith and Solus. The artifacts allowed her to share everything she discovered with them as quickly as a mind link."]},{"number":4508,"title":"Chapter 4508 Not a Hybrid (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Baba Yaga gathered all the information she needed in three breaths, but she checked her findings multiple times, giving the artifacts time to complete their scans. Also, she didn’t want to believe her own findings and hoped the Menadion Set would prove her wrong.","\"It’s your turn, Lith.\" She stepped away and conjured a chair. \"I hope you have better luck.\"","The Crone sat down, trying to make sense of what she had just seen. When Lith approached the pregnant Dryad, she had another fit of rage that forced the arrays to suppress her powers until she calmed down.","This time, the silver flames of mother and child flashed briefly. Light Soul attacked Althika, while Feast Soul infused energy into Light Soul, but no barrier activated to stop either bloodline ability.","The sickly white lights bathed Lith with no effect aside from giving him the creeps.","He used his breathing technique, Abyssal Gaze, and noticed much fewer things than Baba Yaga, yet his diagnosis wasn’t much different. He turned to her and shook his head.","\"Very well.\" The Crone stood up with a sigh. \"I don’t have good news, child, but I need to know what led you to your current condition to be certain of my diagnosis. Lotho mentioned an accident during your training, but didn’t go into details.","\"I assume he’s referring to this.\" Baba Yaga lifted the bedsheet, revealing the unsettling deformity of Althika’s left leg.","Her delicate toes and light green skin had been replaced by curved talons and a thick, black hide covered in bristles. The Crone furrowed her brows, noticing that the Vurdalak flesh covered the Dryad’s leg up to the calf.","When she had used Sun and Moon, only the left foot had been overtaken.","\"Tell me, child, how did this happen, and why didn’t you cure it?\"","\"There isn’t much to say.\" The Dryad gasped, her body tensing as she suppressed another surge of hunger that demanded that she consume the life growing in her womb or at least her own.","\"A few days ago, the silver flame appeared above my and my child’s head. I assumed it was the sign that his development had reached a new milestone and that he had awakened a new bloodline ability for both of us.","\"My clan agreed with me, so I started experimenting with the silver flame while the feeling was still vivid in my mind. I had a vague idea of what I needed to do, like a long-forgotten instinct that necessity had stirred, and I followed it.","\"When I activated the silver flame, however, it gave me no power. It sent my Upyr side into a rampage, and before I could stop it, the Dryad life force of my left foot was gone. It’s also when the hunger appeared for the first time.","\"I didn’t understand what I hungered for at first, and tried to undo the damage to my life force. My regenerating abilities were helpless against the phenomenon, and so were all the healing spells I know.","\"The Elders of the Redleaf family treated me with Body Sculpting, and it worked for some time. My life force still hurt, and the hunger abated, but after a while my foot reverted to its monstrous appearance, and the hunger returned stronger than before.","\"I hoped that stopping the treatments would also stabilize my condition, but it didn’t.\" Althika arched her back in agony, needing sheer willpower to contain the wrath of the Vurdalak that craved to spill Lith’s blood.","\"It only made things worse!\" She started to sob. \"The Upyr life force keeps trying to spread, and my hunger becomes stronger every time I fail to contain it. Now the effects of a Body Sculpting treatment last less than an hour before coming undone.","\"That’s why Naphila called Lotho and asked him to bring you here.\"","\"Is that true, Naphila?\" The Crone squeezed the Titania’s flower, compelling her to answer without omitting anything. \"Did your Elders really do their best, or did they just experiment on Althika?\"","\"We did our best!\" The Head of House Redleaf writhed in agony. \"Our absolute best. We plants are not versed in healing magic, though. We know Body Sculpting but rarely practice it. It was the perfect excuse to lure Verhen here.\"","\"This confirms my suspicions.\" Baba Yaga nodded. \"Sadly, it doesn’t make your situation any better, child. I have only bad news. The silver flames you and your son share are indeed a bloodline ability, but they are not the same.","\"On top of that, they are like nothing I’ve ever seen before. Your silver flame’s purpose, Althika, is not to heal or reinforce the vitality of its user, but to corrupt their life force and turn a Upyr hybrid like you into a Vurdalak.\"","\"What?\" The plant folks and Fae in the room and those listening to the conversation via surveillance mirrors went grey, the sap flushing away from their bark and skin.","\"Are you saying that the Vurdalak bloodline can’t be integrated with the Fae?\" Lotho asked. \"That there is a compatibility issue?\"","\"No, I’m saying that the Vurdalak bloodline can’t be integrated with any bloodline.\" Baba Yaga shook her head. \"An Upyr is not a hybrid as we classify them. It’s a step towards turning someone into a Vurdalak, just like becoming a Thrall precedes turning someone into an undead.","\"The only difference is that the process involves the life force instead of the mana core, and it’s not a voluntary act. The Vurdalak blood is a parasite that enters the host disguised as a symbiote and tries to take over every time you call upon its powers.","\"The silver flame is a bloodline ability meant to facilitate the invasion of the host’s original life force and replace it with the Vurdalak’s. As for your leg, the Body Sculpting procedure would have worked on a regular Upyr.","\"You, however, have a little Vurdalak in your womb. His blood acts as a catalyst, reinforcing your Upyr side and accelerating the takeover with every beat of your heart. What you are experiencing has nothing to do wo with your Fae bloodline. The same fate would befall any woman carrying Meln’s child.\"","\"So, this isn’t the right path to give birth to a plant Divine Beast.\" Naphila gritted her pearly teeth in frustration as her dreams of power shattered. \"The Vurdalak blood would assimilate and replace any of us!\"","\"Correct.\" The Crone replied. \"You can try mixing your bloodlines with normal Divine Beasts, but don’t expect different results from the past.\"","\"What about my hunger?\" Althika asked. \"What’s wrong with me, and why do I feel the compulsion to hurt my own baby?\"","\"Great Mother, help me.\" Baba Yaga sat down, feeling the weight of her next word crushing her. \"To understand your condition, you must know that Night is no expert on life forces nor a scholar.","\"She’s a tinkerer at best, and not a good one at that. At first glance, one might think she took Orpal’s human, Dragon, and Vampire bloodlines and fused them in a pale imitation of a Tiamat.","\"That somehow, things went wrong in the merging and harmonizing of the different life forces, and they all turned undead.\" It was the Black Throne’s conclusion, but Baba Yaga knew better."]},{"number":4509,"title":"Chapter 4509 Hollow Being (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"I wish that were true. It would make things much easier. The reality is that my rebellious daughter cut the different aspects of Orpal’s life force apart with the grace of a butcher and then stitched together what was left.\" Baba Yaga said.","\"If not for Night’s regenerative abilities, Orpal would have never survived the process. The Vurdalak that he has become is not a stable Divine Beast bloodline nor an undead. It’s an aberration.","\"A living disease, akin to a cancer that, after replacing all the healthy tissues, also replaces its host. What you are experiencing, Althika, is the hunger typical of my children, but it has been twisted and perverted beyond recognition.","\"Undead need the life essence of their race’s members to prolong their existence and never forget their origin. Vurdalaks, instead, are living beings; they should have no reason to feed on their kin.","\"Yet Night’s crazy experiments have left the Vurdalak life force incomplete. There are gaping holes in its structure that need to be filled. Check your son’s Vurdalak life force, if you don’t believe me.","\"There is no trace of the mana organs of the human, Dragon, and Vampire bloodline. Nothing. He’s an empty slate that tries to fill the blanks with the Dryad bloodline.\"","Lith’s eyes widened in shock, and the other people in the room fared no better.","\"Can you please show us what we missed?\" Lith and Lotho asked.","\"Please, Lady Yaga, show me as well! I need to know!\" Naphila begged in frustration and despair.","Althika and the Crone nodded, and the three examined the Dryad with their respective breathing techniques under the Crone’s guidance. What they found confirmed her words. Even the unborn child wasn’t safe from the Vurdalak blood.","If not for his Dryad side’s regenerative abilities, his life force would have already been assimilated.","\"Would my child still retain his bloodline abilities after becoming a full-blooded Vurdalak?\" Althika asked.","\"No.\" The Crone replied in disgust. \"As I said, a Vurdalak is a mangled, corrupted creature. At best, your son would retain a couple of his Dryad mana organs, and they would become twisted and corrupted.","\"Everything of you that makes your son would be remade in Meln’s image.\"","\"What about my hunger?\" The Dryad pressed on. \"What does this have to do with my hunger?\"","\"Everything.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"As Vurdalaks, you and your son are incomplete beings that crave to become whole. The hunger you experience is a symptom of your condition.","\"The silver fire on your baby’s head, instead, is the means to resolve it. It allows a Vurdalak to prey on a fellow Vurdalak, assimilating their energy and any mana organ they have acquired until that moment.","\"While my children feed on the living, the Vurdalak bloodline feeds on itself until there’s no hole left in the life force. A normal Upyr would be spared from the hunger until their transformation into a Vurdalak is complete, Althika, but your case is different.","\"The baby’s Vurdalak blood that flows in your veins allows his silver flame and yours to synergize in a loop. They are constantly eroding your mind and body, inflicting upon you the worst of both worlds.","\"Even if you never practiced the silver flame, it was only a matter of time before you ended up like this. In the same way, it’s only a matter of time before your Upyr side swallows your Dryad life force and you become a Vurdalak.\"","\"Wait a moment.\" Lith pondered. \"Why didn’t Meln suffer from this hunger before? If he’s anything like your children, he should have died of starvation by now.\"","\"He’s nothing like my children!\" Baba Yaga snarled. \"He’s alive, and can eat normal food to survive. The hunger is only a byproduct of Night’s incompetence, and it spurs a Vurdalak to finish the job she half-assed.","\"I bet Meln didn’t experience any hunger until my plan with the Harmonizer backfired and turned one of his Upyrs into a full Vurdalak. He had always been the only member of his species, so nothing could trigger his primal instinct.","\"It explains everything. Why my plan failed, why the Vurdalak I unwittingly created attacked Meln’s Chosen, and why Meln retreated like that. He had already gained more than he came for and needed time to study his new powers.","\"It also matches the timing of Althika’s transformation. This is all my fault.\"","\"Did you do this?\" The Dryad snarled, her teeth shapeshifting into needle-like fangs. \"Did you do this to my child, you dumb bitch?\"","\"I’m afraid so.\" Baba Yaga sighed. \"Which makes what I’m about to say even harder. I can fix your corrupted life force, child. I can restore your Dryad side to perfection and cleanse the illness, but that won’t last long.","\"The small Vurdalak in your womb will keep spreading his cursed blood through your body, and sooner or later you’ll be like this again, if not worse. My recommendation is to kill mother and child.\"","\"Althika as well?\" Lotho was flabbergasted. \"Why? Didn’t you just say you can cure her, Lady Yaga?\"","\"I did, and I can, but she would still be a Upyr.\" The Crone replied. \"Her life force would still be under the relentless attack of the Vurdalak’s blood. One day, maybe when her life is in danger, or she’s under great stress, Althika’ll lose control.","\"She’ll become a Vurdalak, and then we’d have another Meln to deal with. You’ve seen how Althika reacted when she saw Lith. You’ve heard the Dead King’s voice coming out of her mouth.\"","\"About that.\" Lotho pondered. \"How is that possible? Althika didn’t take Meln’s blood. She became a Upyr through her unborn son.\"","\"And how do you think that child got there?\" Baba Yaga replied. \"Althika still took part of the Dead King’s life essence inside her. It wasn’t enough to turn her in a Upyr, but it infected her with his madness.","\"The Vurdalak blood of the baby turned her body into fertile soil, and the madness took deep root in her Upyr side. The baby has been spared from it, but only because his own Vurdalak blood protected him from the infection.","\"Althika’s Upyr side, instead, is a mindless creature driven only by instinct. Whatever part of himself Meln left inside Althika’s body had an easy time possessing it since the baby never tried to manipulate his mother.\"","\"Are you sure about this?\" Lotho said after checking the Dryad again and again. \"I find no anomaly in Althika’s life force.\"","\"It’s hard to notice, but Lady Yaga is right.\" Lith said. \"There is a faint trace of Meln’s corruption.\"","’Yet it’s so faint that we missed it with Demon Grasp.’ Solus said. ’If not for the Ears and the Eyes of Menadion, we’d have never noticed it.’","The artifacts displayed a faint black light coursing throughout the Dryad’s body. Not a single hair had been spared from the affliction.","\"Is there nothing you can do?\" Althika sobbed.","\"I can try removing the madness, but it’s so widespread that the procedure would maim your life force.\" Baba Yaga said. \"Even if you survived, there wouldn’t be enough left of you to have a life or retain your personality.\""]},{"number":4510,"title":"Chapter 4510 Hollow Being (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"You’d be crippled in mind and body. To what degree, it’s impossible to say. The choice is yours, but if you ask me, death is the most merciful solution. Unless you want the Vurdalak bloodline to spread.","\"To let this cancer turn parent against child, brother against sibling, and clan leader against their people. Vurdalaks only see each other as food. They are incapable of trusting their own kin because being close to them causes the hunger you’re experiencing, child.","\"Do you wish that on your clan or any other living being?\" The Crone asked.","\"No.\" Althika cried, battling the despair ravaging her heart.","She was about to die, and every egotistical instinct she had screamed for her to satisfy her hunger and run away. Yet she refused to listen, preferring to die with dignity as Althika the Dryad rather than as a monstrous Vurdalak.","\"I don’t want this for anyone. Especially my baby boy. Is he suffering? Does he feel what I feel?\"","\"It’s likely.\" The Crone nodded. \"Just like you, however, he refuses to yield. The curse left by his father has yet to overpower the baby’s desire to protect you.\"","\"Verhen?\" Althika turned to Lith. \"Is there nothing you can do?\"","’He’s younger and much less knowledgeable than Baba Yaga, but I won’t surrender my child’s life until there is a single shred of hope left.’ She thought.","\"I think I can save you.\" Lith replied, shocking everyone. \"I think I can save you both.\"","\"How?\" Baba Yaga asked. \"This is my first time seeing something like this, and I doubt you ever encountered an illness remotely similar, let alone treated it.\"","\"It’s my first time as well, yet I know there’s something I can do.\" Lith’s face was a mask of focus as he searched inside himself for the right words. \"It’s an instinct similar to when I helped Solus or Ely helped Zoreth.","\"Ever since I touched Althika, I can hear two voices in my head. One repeats, kill, obsessively. The other screams, wrong, over and over.\"","\"An instinct?\" Lotho scoffed.","\"You hear voices?\" Naphila sneered, and the Crone squeezed her Root into a crumpled mess to shut her up.","\"Are you sure?\" Baba Yaga asked. \"I’m not doubting you. I know who you are and what you are capable of. I just want to make sure you realize how much is at stake here. You risk destroying three lives if you are wrong.","\"Althika’s, her son’s, and your own. Can you live with the consequences of your actions if you fail?\"","\"I don’t know.\" Lith shook his head. \"The only thing I’m certain is that I won’t be able to live with myself if I don’t at least try. I can’t promise you anything, Althika. I can’t give you an explanation or my odds of success.","\"I can only assure you that I’m not lying when I say that I believe I can help you. Whether to believe me is your choice.\"","\"Nice move, Leech!\" The Dryad’s delicate features twisted into a Vurdalak who spoke with Orpal’s voice. \"You get to kill my child and pose as a hero. Only if this idiot buys your act, though!\"","Baba Yaga used the arrays of the lair to restrain Althika before she assaulted Lith and used her tier five Body Sculpting spell, Cradle of Life, to suppress the influence of Orpal’s fragment over the Dryad’s mind and Light Soul before the corruption of the Vurdalak’s flesh spread further.","\"Do everything you can.\" Althika panted heavily as she now had to fight back both the hunger and the attempts of the Dead King’s fragment to possess her. \"Just promise me that if it comes down to a choice between my baby and me, you’ll save my son.","\"I put us in this spot, whereas he’s innocent.\"","\"On that, we agree.\" Lith replied. \"Lady Yaga, make sure that nobody disturbs me. I can’t afford my focus to slip even for one second. Also, no matter the outcome, once I’m done, I’ll be helpless and in need of your protection.\"","\"Leave that to me.\" A wave of the Crone’s hand depowered most of the arrays of the Redleaf Clan, flooding Bloodhaven and Starforge with all the world energy they needed.","She and Solus conjured the magical formations of the towers to seal the medical ward from any external influence.","\"Whenever you are ready.\"","\"Okay, Meln, this is between you and me, like usual.\" Lith moved to the Dryad’s bedside and took deep, slow breaths. \"The only difference is that this time you can’t run away like you always do.\"","Then he turned to Althika.","\"This may hurt a lot, and for that, I’m sorry. I need you to be brave and not struggle, no matter how scary it gets, okay?\"","\"Okay.\" She nodded, too busy holding the Light Soul under control to feel any fear.","\"Now, close your eyes.\" Lith said, and Althika did as bidden.","Only then did he unfurl his six wings and use the world energy he absorbed through them to wreath himself in Dread Flames. Lith placed his right thumb in the middle of the Dryad’s forehead and his left thumb above her heart.","The moment he touched her skin, he could hear the voices inside his head clearly enough to distinguish them.","’Wrong!’ The Voidfeather Dragon roared. ’It’s all wrong! Wrong!’","’Kill!’ The Void hissed. ’Kill it now! Leave nothing behind!’","’Make up your mind, dammit!’ Lith struggled to tune the voices down and focus on the readings of the Eyes and the Ears. ’First, I need to get rid of Meln’s influence. That thing is alive and can somehow reason.","’If I let it be, there’s no telling how it might screw up the rest of the procedure. Althika might survive thanks to her regenerative abilities, but the baby’s life force is much weaker. All it takes is one mistake, and the Dread Flames will kill him.’","Lith opened his mouth, exhaling a slow stream of silvery flames as thin as a hair that struck where the black mist of Orpal’s influence was thickest. Althika clenched her teeth in agony as her flesh burned, while the black mist reeled at the contact.","Lith heard Orpal scream in pain amid the distorted melody of the Dryad’s life force, but it only lasted a second. Her regenerative abilities instantly closed the wound, and the black mist moved away from the silvery flames.","Lith tried a few more times, but the result was always the same. The black mist dodged the flames by using Althika’s body as a literal meat shield and exploiting her healing factor to cover its escape.","’The damage I do to Meln’s fragment is negligible. I’m draining Althika’s vitality and mental focus for nothing. Solus?’","’Neither the Eyes nor the Ears are a diagnostic instrument.’ She replied. ’They are meant for Forgemastering processes. It’s the reason Mom dedicated an entire floor of the tower to the Infirmary.","’There’s only so much I can tell you unless we put Althika in the crystal tank.’","’And expose the tower’s existence to the rest of Mogar? Thanks, but no thanks. We’ve already seen how the plant folk’s idea of gratitude is a knife in our back.’"]},{"number":4511,"title":"Chapter 4511 Lifting the Veil (Part 1)","paragraphs":["’Moreover, the Infirmary can only help us to understand the illness, and we already know what it is. Finding a cure is up to us anyway.’ Not knowing what else to do, Lith stopped breathing the Dread Flames and fighting the voices in his head.","The Voidfeather Dragon spoke the loudest. He guided Lith to flood his eyes with the power of the elements and then focus on what he saw through his Spirit Eye.","Spirit Vision showed him the Dryad and the Upyr life forces, where they overlapped, and brought into focus what the Ears of Menadion perceived as a thin fog.","A sickly black substance moved from the Upyr side to the Dryad, attacking Althika’s original life force and retreating as soon as her regenerative abilities triggered in response to the invasion.","Orpal’s fragment moved with purpose, striking at the first moment of weakness and hiding behind the Upyr life force whenever it was attacked.","’That’s why I failed until now.’ Lith was flabbergasted. ’That thing is not static. I can’t just pin it down and burn it to the ground. I need-’","’Not burn. Kill!’ The Void cut him short. ’Like this.’","The crown of fire on top of Lith’s head turned blue as he opened the cracks in his life force just enough to ignite Death Vision and a spark of Scourge Flames. Spirit Vision showed him the different aspects of the Dryad’s life force, while Death Vision showed Lith how they could die.","He took one last deep breath and exhaled three tiny streams of fire. The Scourge Flames advanced toward Orpal’s essence with one stream of Dread Flames on either side.","The blue fire ignited the black substance, and it once again tried to escape. This time, however, there was no way out. The Scourge Flames never let go of their prey, while the Dread Flames flanked both hunter and prey.","Orpal’s essence could run, but it couldn’t hide any longer. The Scourge Flames marked its position at all times, and the Dread Flames kept it from moving inside the healthy tissues.","The first black droplet died with an agonizing scream, and the hunt began anew. Baba Yaga’s assessment of Althika’s condition was correct. Orpal’s essence had spread all over the Dryad’s life force, infecting every nook and cranny of her body.","It covered her healthy tissues like a spiderweb. Thin, but incredibly sturdy, and easy to burn. Lith cleansed the black substance one rivulet at a time, until Althika’s head belonged to her again.","The Dead King had no influence over her anymore, and resisting the hunger became easier. Then Lith cleansed her chest, her arms, and her right leg, leaving the left leg for last.","\"Clench your teeth. This is going to hurt a lot.\" Lith waited for the Dryad to nod before letting the Scourge Flames run wild on the Vurdalak foot. They burned the deformed flesh and bones, purging the Dryad’s life force of its corruption.","Althika held on for a few seconds before she screamed at the top of her lungs. Her flesh burned, her blood boiled, and her very soul seemed to have fallen in a pool of lava.","The Vurdalak flesh blacked into a charred mass and fell to the ground in a pile of ashes. Althika’s body regenerated the missing limb as soon as the Scourge Flames went out, shaping it out of fast-growing vines.","\"That’s my foot!\" The Dryad opened her eyes to admire her delicate toes and the uniform green of her skin. \"That thing is gone! I’m me again!\"","At the same time, in the fortress of Nareka in Jiera, Orpal clutched his chest in agony, sharing the searing demise of his fragment and feeling that a small part of him was gone forever.","\"How is the hunger?\" Lith leaned against the nearest wall and let himself slide down until he was sitting on the floor.","\"It’s gone!\" Althika looked at the Light Soul above her head and discovered it had shrunk to a candlelight. \"I’m cured, and so is my baby!\"","The unborn child’s Feast Soul also had stopped blazing and was reduced to a spark.","\"I wish that were true, child.\" Baba Yaga sighed. \"You’re not cured. It’s just that, like an undead can only feed on those who belong to their original race, a Vurdalak preys only on other Vurdalaks.","\"You’re back to being an Upyr, and as such you can no longer use or be a victim of the bloodline ability Vurdalaks use to consume each other.\"","\"It’s still good news, right?\" The Dryad appreciated every breath she took, no longer feeling pain coming from her left leg or the hunger eroding her sanity. \"I’m stable again, and my child is no longer in danger.\"","\"I’m sorry, but that’s wishful thinking.\" The Crone replied. \"You are still an Upyr and carry a Vurdalak in your womb. Your Dryad life force is under constant attack, and it’s only a matter of time before stress or strain makes you fall again.","\"At that point, the bloodline ability will return, and so will the hunger. Depending on the situation, the next time you might not be able to resist the transformation and become a full-blooded Vurdalak. I let you imagine the rest.\"","\"What if I remain in isolation until I give birth?\" Althika asked. \"If I don’t put myself in danger, there won’t be any stressful situation, right?\"","\"Childbirth is no walk in the park, child.\" Baba Yaga shook her head. \"Even assuming your clan plays nice, which I find hard to believe, once the labor begins, your body will undergo plenty of strain.","\"If the transformation happens at such a delicate moment, Lith wouldn’t be able to do anything even if he stood right by your side. Yet even if everything goes fine, that won’t be the end of your trouble.","\"You may be allowed to spend the rest of your life in isolation, but do you think your son will accept such fate? Do you think the Council, or any of the five races for that matter, will allow a living plague to endure?\"","\"Then what was the point of dousing me with those flames?\" Althika cried tears of desperation. \"Why didn’t you just put me down like the rabid monster you say I am?\"","\"Because that was just the first step of your treatment.\" Lith’s ragged breath slowly returned to normal as the energy from Starforge stabilized his life force and restored his strength. \"I’m not done yet. I’m just catching my breath.","\"You’d better focus on refilling your body with nutrients, because you’re going to need them soon.\"","The Dryad nodded and extended several vines from her hands. They seeped into the wooden floor, absorbing everything she needed to return to her peak condition.","\"We’re lucky you’re a plant folk, Althika.\" Lith said, his voice still punctuated by short gasps. \"I don’t think I could have performed this procedure on any other race. At least not alone.","\"Sure, Lady Yaga would’ve helped me to heal your wounds, but coordinating our efforts would have made things much more complicated. I don’t know what to expect from the procedure, and if Lady Yaga asked me to stop at a critical moment, I don’t know if I could.\""]},{"number":4512,"title":"Chapter 4512 Lifting the Veil (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Why are you telling me this?\" The Dryad swallowed hard. \"Are you trying to scare me?\"","\"I’m trying to reassure you.\" He took a deep breath, checking the strength of his life force and testing his ability to focus. \"You’re the perfect patient, Althika. If anyone can survive this, it’s you.","\"Are you ready to begin the second step of your treatment?\"","\"What about my baby?\" She asked, placing her hands on her swollen womb to protect it.","\"I won’t even come close to him.\" Lith replied. \"He’ll be safe. You have my word.\"","Althika used her breathing technique to check on the small life growing inside her, and her heartbeat steadied after listening to her son’s.","\"I’m ready.\" She nodded. \"Do I need to close my eyes again?\"","\"Meln can no longer interfere, but I’d rather you not watch. As Lady Yaga said, let’s avoid pointless stress.\"","\"Okay.\" The Dryad leaned her head against the pillow and closed her eyes, trying to convince herself she was just about to take a nap.","Lith placed his hands on her forehead and chest again and listened to the other aspects of his life force.","’Wrong! This is wrong!’ The Voidfeather Dragon was still loud and angry, while the Void had gone silent.","A deep breath ignited the Dread Flames, and a second breath wreathed Lith in them, covering him from head to toe.","\"Listen to me, Althika. No matter what happens, don’t fight me. Fight him.\" Lith’s words made no sense to her until the Dread Flames seeped inside her body.","They phased through the Dryad life force without harming it and encroached on the Upyr side. As a hybrid, Althika had one mana core and two distinct life forces that weren’t supposed to overlap.","In her case, however, the Upyr had silently invaded the Dryad side, and the two life forces presented several contact points. Lith focused the Dread Flames there, burning the Upyr life force even at the cost of harming part of the contaminated Dryad side.","Althika clenched her teeth in pain, but followed Lith’s instructions and kept her regenerative abilities in check. Her Dryad life force remained still, accepting the Dread Flames’ liberating touch as it drove the Upyr side away.","\"Now you can heal.\" Lith said. \"Tap my hand once you are done.\"","Althika nodded and tapped his hand.","\"Now, fight with me.\" Lith released one more breath of silvery flames, and this time it was a sword, not a scalpel.","It cut deep into the Upyr life force, opening a path that the Dryad side exploited to invade its hated enemy. The Upyr side fought back, but new tongues of Dread Flames burned it down and cleared new paths for the Dryad life force.","Every time Lith killed part of her Upyr side, Althika felt pain, but it was a pleasant kind of pain, like bursting a boil or sewing an open wound close. It was the kind of pain that promised the end of suffering, and was followed by relief as her tissues healed.","Lith destroyed the Upyr life force one burst of Dread Flames at a time, allowing the Dryad side to reclaim Althika’s body piece by piece. Once the treatment ended, she was no longer a Divine Beast.","She felt weaker than she had in months, and her body seemed to have turned into trembling jelly. The loss of her raw physical might pained her plant folk’s innate thirst for power as a real wound, but she didn’t care.","She also wasn’t corrupted anymore. With her Upyr side gone, the veil cast by Orpal’s bloodline was lifted from her eyes. Althika could think freely again and finally realized the steep price she had paid in her dogged quest to become a Divine Beast.","\"Gods!\" She cried warm tears of relief and regret. \"What have I done? What have I become? How could I have been so stupid?\"","\"That’s how corruption works, child.\" Baba Yaga wiped the sap-sweat off the Dryad’s face and caressed her hand. \"Only evil people and those who just pretend to be good fall into its clutches in one go.","\"Stupid people like you, instead, start by taking a small bite, telling themselves it’s not a big deal, and they can stop anytime. Then they take another, and a bigger one next, until they get so used to the taste that they consider it normal.","\"That’s how most people fall into corruption without even noticing. You take one step away from your original self until you’re not able to see what you looked like anymore and convince yourself you’ve always been like that.\"","Being called stupid hurt the Dryad’s pride, but realizing the depth of her stupidity was much worse.","\"How do you feel?\" Lith was back sitting on the floor, his breathing more ragged than before.","\"Stupid.\" Althika sniffled as tears and snot ran down her face. \"Like the dumbest person on Mogar. Yet I know that’s not what you’re asking. I feel better than fine. I feel like I’ve been born again.\"","\"That’s good.\" Lith took a barrel of tonics and gulped it down.","\"I’m sorry for raining on your parade, but I need to ask.\" Baba Yaga said. \"What’s the point of this? Althika will revert into a Upyr in a few months, if not even weeks. You’ve solved nothing; you’ve just delayed the inevitable.\"","Those words hit the Dryad like a slap and made Lotho’s eyes go wide.","\"She’s right.\" The Treant’s voice sounded like the rustling of leaves. \"The baby’s Vurdalak blood is always flowing through her veins, and she gets more by the second. The more the baby develops, the faster her transformation will be.\"","Althika bent forward in a defensive position, shielding her child from those she now realized would always be her enemies.","\"I know that.\" Lith replied. \"I never said I’m done. I’m just recovering before I start the third step of her treatment.\"","\"The third step?\" Althika echoed in disbelief. \"The Dead King’s fragment is destroyed, and I’m no longer an Upyr. What are you-\"","The words died on her lips as she reached the only possible answer to her own question.","\"My baby? You want to breathe your cruel fire on my baby?\"","\"No, I promised you that I would save your baby, and that’s what I’m going to do.\" Lith replied.","\"Save how?\" Althika snarled. \"He’s too small and weak! He’s not like me. I was never supposed to have a Upyr side, whereas my son Vurdalak’s side is an integral part of him. He’ll die if you burn away half of his life force.\"","\"Have you forgotten what Lady Yaga said after examining you?\" Lith’s voice was calm, yet there was no warmth in it. \"What she recommended us to do? Your child is a threat to every form of life on Mogar. He’s the seed of a plague waiting to spread itself.\"","\"I know, but-\"","\"There’s no but.\" Lith cut her short. \"If you send me away, your son will be hunted down all his life. There will be people who want his blood for themselves and those who want to kill him, yet no matter who finds him first, he’ll never know peace.\""]},{"number":4513,"title":"Chapter 4513 Two Decades Old Daydream (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Even if you keep your son safe, what do you think will happen once he grows up? How will you explain to him why he’s not allowed to fall in love, tell others about his heritage, or have children of his own?\" Lith asked.","Althika’s rage died, and her face turned pale green. Tears of desperation streaked down her cheeks; the joy she had experienced a few seconds ago for being freed of the Vurdalak blood seemed a distant memory already.","\"I’m sorry, child, but I haven’t changed my mind.\" Baba Yaga bowed her head deeply in apology. \"Lith is right. We can’t allow a Vurdalak to live. No matter whose child they might be.\"","\"How many times do I have to say that I’m not going to kill the baby?\" Lith snarled. \"I won’t deny that once I step on the battlefield, I become a murderer, but this is a hospital ward, and I’ve come here as a Healer.","\"My role is to protect lives, all kinds of lives. Not to take them.\"","\"Is this your instinct talking?\" The Crone asked, and Lith nodded in reply. \"Then even you have no idea what you’re about to do, I’ll trust you. You’ve already done what I considered impossible twice, child. You can do it a third time.\"","\"Can I say something?\" Lotho asked.","\"No.\" Lith, Baba Yaga, and Althika snorted in unison.","The Crone activated the arrays of the towers and the underground complex, sending all the Fae in the building crashing against the ground and sending the message that their opinion didn’t matter, especially Naphila’s.","\"Althika?\" Lith asked. \"I need your permission since I can’t ask your baby’s. If you want me to leave, I’ll leave. I’m a parent as well, yet I can only imagine what you’re going through.\"","\"You’re not sure you’ll succeed. You don’t even know what you’re doing, right?\" She asked, and Lith shook his head. \"Do you really believe you can... heal my son?\"","\"I do. Just like I believed I could save you a few minutes ago.\" Lith replied.","\"Then I’ll entrust my child’s life to you as I entrusted mine. Do everything you can.\" The Dryad said.","\"Replenish your strength first.\" Lith pointed at the wooden floor. \"I don’t know how long it will take or how hard it will be. He’s going to need your help.\"","Althika absorbed the nutrients from the ground and used her breathing technique to metabolize them rapidly until the fatigue from her treatments disappeared.","\"I’m ready.\" She said, feeling as if she had just returned from a relaxing vacation.","\"I’m not.\" Lith replied. \"It might take a while before I start the third and final step of the treatment. I need you to remain silent and not disturb me unless it’s an emergency.\"","Nobody understood what he meant, but they nodded anyway. Life Vision showed Baba Yaga that Lith’s mana core and life force were back at their peak condition.","’The Infirmary confirms it. Lith is physically fine and capable of harnessing Starforge’s power.’ Solus said.","’Then what’s the issue?’ Baba Yaga asked, but Solus didn’t answer.","’By my Mom, I wish I could stand by Lith’s side.’ She thought, being careful that he couldn’t overhear her. ’The baby may be innocent, but he’s still Meln’s son. Lith must be torn at the idea of helping his despised brother’s bloodline thrive.","’It’s petty and mean, but it’s also a natural feeling after everything Meln put Lith and our family through. I’d give anything to stand by his side and share his burden, but this is something he must do alone.","’One of the biggest issues in our relationship is that we are codependent. We often do things not because we want to or believe they’re the right thing to do, only because it’s what the other wants.","’We care so much about each other’s feelings that we often end up trampling our own to make the other happy. I’m not leaving Lith alone. I’m taking a step back because I trust him and I know that if he needs my help, he will ask me.’","’Fuck me sideways, helping Meln’s offspring is only half of the equation.’ Lith thought. ’The other half is that if my focus strays even for one second or I hesitate in a critical moment, the procedure will fail and the baby will die.","’Bringing myself to do this is not enough. I must put my mind, heart, and soul in it. Or everything will be for nothing. The others may believe me when I say I did everything I could, but I’ll know the truth.","’How could I look my kids and lead them by example when-’ His train of thought didn’t derail; it switched tracks. ’That’s it. Listen to me, brain, I’m not helping a stupid, power-hungry Dryad keep Meln’s son alive.","’I’m helping Carl’s fiancée keep his son alive. I even know the little imp’s name. Carl always said that he would have called his first child Erik if it were a male. Remember this, Derek McCoy: you’re saving your nephew, Erik.’","Lith cleared his mind of stray thoughts and delved into a daydream over two decades old. He had pictured that moment so many times that it was as clear as a real memory.","Carl’s old fiancée lying in a hospital bed after giving birth, exhausted but happy. Carl staying by her side, excited yet terrified as he held his son. That was the moment when, in his imagination, Derek walked through the door.","He could see Carl showing off the little bundle of joy named Erik before offering his brother to be the first to hold the baby boy after his parents. Lith focused on that imaginary moment and let it overlap with the memory of holding Elysia for the first time.","Her warmth became Erik’s warmth. Her weight that Lith still vividly remembered became the baby boy’s weight. Reality and illusion merged into one as Lith opened his eyes, all seven of them.","He knew who and where he was. He was aware of how dangerous the procedure was. The only difference from one second ago was that Meln’s very existence had been banished from his mind.","Dread Flames burst out of his body, burning high and seeping deep. The layer of scales that usually covered his red skin was gone, replaced by the searing silvery fire.","Lith remained still for a few, long minutes, staring at Althika’s swollen womb as if trying to decipher the mysteries of life and death. In a way, he was. Spirit Vision locked in on the baby’s Vurdalak life force, and then went deeper.","Until that moment, Lith had always let the Voidfeather Dragon lead him in the use of the unknown ability and relied on Spirit Vision to study how life forces and mana cores interacted.","That wasn’t enough. Not anymore. Lith focused solely on the life force and pushed Spirit Vision to the limit, forcing it to reveal what happened beneath the surface. He memorized how many sections comprised the Vurdalak life force, the number and position of mana organs, and how every element interacted with its surroundings.","The life force looked like a molten, spherical contraption made from junk parts fused together with a blowtorch."]},{"number":4514,"title":"Chapter 4514 Two Decades Old Daydream (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Jagged blocks and barbed wires that oozed a black substance filled the molten sphere, with six volcano-like protuberances forming a ring around it.","The sphere didn’t burn so much as liquefied and reformed as the volcanoes erupted, each spreading a different kind of sickly light. The molten sphere changed its color accordingly, often turning grey when too many volcanoes erupted together.","The melody of the Vurdalak, instead, was a discordant mess of flat notes. It sounded as if a group of teens had put together a band even though none of them had ever played an instrument.","There was no harmony, tune, or feeling to it. It was a cacophony of noise that desperately wanted to be music, but didn’t know the first thing about it. Like a spoiled kid who believed putting on a lab coat would miracolously grant him the skill of a real doctor.","Lith saw and heard everything, but the thought that such life force and its melody fit everything he knew about Orpal didn’t cross his mind. He was a Healer, and he faced that monstrosity like he would a disease that distorted his patient’s healthy life force and the melody it produced.","Spirit Vision broke complex structures down into their components, scanning every nook and cranny of the Vurdalak’s essence. Lith checked his findings over and over, until he understood what he was against and what he had to do.","He leaned forward, putting both hands on Althika’s womb and leaning so close to it that she could feel his breath on her skin. Yet neither his touch nor presence burned. The Dryad felt as if someone had covered her with a warm blanket to protect her from a winter storm.","’Don’t worry, Carl, your big brother is here.’ Lith thought as he retracted his face mask and opened his mouth. ’This time, I won’t let anyone ruin your happiness.’","He exhaled a gentle, placid stream of Dread Flames that split into several small rivulets upon touching the baby’s Vurdalak life force. Althika and her unborn child felt nothing, the silvery flame as ethereal as mist.","Lith kept breathing until every lick of fire was in position and perfectly balanced. Baba Yaga and Solus followed his work closely, and to them, it looked like the life force had been caught in a fiery, irregular fishing net.","Lith studied the Vurdalak life force one last time, and unleashed the full power of the Dread Flames on it. They burned along the junction lines that connected the edges of the different parts, eating at Night’s demented Body Sculpting modifications from every side.","The Dread Flames didn’t affect the life force directly. Their purpose wasn’t to harm the Vurdalak, but to destroy everything that gave it shape and purpose. Althika felt a sting, a reflection of her baby’s discomfort.","It was painful, but not cruel. Like a needle used to take a blood sample or place an IV. Althika prayed to the gods for help and begged them to protect her son.","At the same time, in the Blood Desert, the many documents floating around Salaark’s desk fell to the floor. The Overlord’s eyes went wide in disquiet and confusion as the events taking place inside the Redleaf Household drew her attention.","She turned to look in that direction, but her desk was in the way. When Salaark stood up from her chair, her knees gave out, and she needed to lean on her desk not to fall to the ground.","Leegaain experienced something similar, but much worse. The Gorgon Empire was his turf, and he could witness the events with his breathing technique, Worldkeeper, as if he were standing right beside Althika.","His vision blurred, and he felt dizzy as his mind spun in a whirlwind of fear and excitement. The Father of All Dragons tried and failed to sit down, falling butt-first against the stone floor of his lab.","Leegaain needed sheer willpower to turn towards the Redleaf Household, and what he saw squeezed the air out of his lungs.","Meanwhile, Lith kept breathing Dread Flames and watching the progress of his work with Spirit Vision, altering the intensity and flow of the flames as the Vurdalak life force slowly collapsed.","Lith kept releasing a constant stream of Dread Flames that burned, severed, and cauterized. He kept the Spirit Eye focused to the extreme, detecting the smallest changes in his patient as soon as they manifested and adapting the treatment accordingly.","Lith’s willpower was laser-focused in the Dread Flames to the point that its countless tendrils moved like the most elite army on Mogar. They attacked, stopped, and repositioned themselves with peerless teamwork and dogged determination.","Althika, however, had no way to know any of this. The silvery fire kept stinging at her, and she was aware that she only experienced a fraction of what her unborn baby was enduring.","To make matters worse, weakness spread from her womb to the rest of her body like a silent disease. More strength abandoned her by the second, and staying awake required all the focus she could muster.","The Dryad could feel in her heart that she was losing something precious and that she would never get it back.","Lith stopped the procedure, recalling what was left of the Dread Flames inside his body, and Althika realized that her greatest fear had become true. After losing her Upyr life force, her mass was back to being that of a Dryad, yet she felt as if her body had turned to lead.","Moving a finger was a struggle, and even heaving her chest to breathe was torture. Every fiber of her being screamed in exhaustion and begged for the sweet release of slumber.","If not for the Crone rushing to the Dryad’s side and using Sun and Moon to restore her vitality, Althika would have lost consciousness.","\"It is done.\" There was finality in Lith’s voice, but mostly sadness and remorse. \"I-\"","\"I’ve lost my child.\" Two tears streaked down the Dryad’s cheeks, plopping on her bedsheets. \"I know something happened to him because I can’t feel his strength anymore. I’m empty. Emptier than I’ve ever been, in mind and soul.\"","Althika sobbed, her tears forming rivulets on her face.","\"You’ve done the best you could, but the curse of the Dead King was too strong.\"","\"No.\" Lith spoke loud enough to drown the Dryad’s voice, his face tense. \"I kept my promise. Your son is alive.\"","\"What?\" Lotho, Althika, and Naphila said in unison.","Baba Yaga Hushed the Treant and squeezed the Titania’s flower so they wouldn’t disturb the grieving Dryad again.","\"Then why do I feel so weak?\" She wailed so hard that her words were barely understandable. \"Why do I feel like I’ve lost something important? Why do I feel so empty?\"","\"Because your son is no longer a Divine Beast.\" Lith said, his words freezing even the clan elders in shock. \"He’s now a healthy human child. Check on him yourself if you don’t believe me.\"","Althika wiped her snot and used her breathing technique to visualize the contents of her womb.","\"Thank the gods, you are right!\" She said, new tears running down her face, but this time filled with joy."]},{"number":4515,"title":"Chapter 4515 One Drop (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"My baby boy is alive. He’s perfect, and all those disgusting flames don’t torment him any longer. How did you do that? I thought your flames were meant to burn and destroy.\" The Dryad asked.","\"That’s what I also believed, child, and the reason I once called Lith, the Destroyer.\" The Crone caressed Althika’s hand with her thumb. \"We were both wrong. His silvery flames are meant to cleanse what’s been tainted and right what’s crooked.","\"Lith’s Dread Flames only burned my mad daughter’s demented magic that forced the life forces of your baby to take the form of a Vurdalak. Lith has freed them from their cage and let them revert to their original state as if nothing wrong has ever happened to them.\"","\"Life forces?\" The Dryad echoed in disbelief. \"Do you mean my baby boy has more than one?\"","\"I... may have glossed over a small detail.\" The sadness and regret in Lith’s voice became palpable. \"Your unborn child is not just a human. He’s a human baby who carries one drop of Phoenix blood and another of Dragon blood.","\"He’s no different from the baby my cursed brother would have if he never turned into a Vurdalak. Your son carries a life force similar to Leria’s, my niece, or any of Rena’s children. In other words, he’s a Verhen.\"","The thought of associating his family name with Orpal’s spawn disgusted Lith, but he still retained enough of his self-induced illusion to speak those words without letting his feelings transpire.","Lith still considered the unborn baby to be Carl’s child, Erik. On top of that, his earlier conversation with Elina was still vivid in his mind. He had promised not to poison his family against Trion, and the baby was no different.","’No matter the circumstances of his conception, the little guy is a Verhen. Mom will cry with joy when she learns that at least part of her lost son is alive and that she has a second chance to save him.’","\"Really?\" Althika smiled from the bottom of her heart. \"Then my bad feelings were just caused by my stupid, power-hungry Dryad instinct! I wasn’t grieving the loss of my son, only the loss of the powers his Divine Beast side gave to me.\"","\"I’m afraid that’s the case, child.\" Baba Yaga gave the Dryad a warm smile.","\"Are you serious?\" Since Naphila was still squirming on the floor, one of the Elders took it upon himself to enter the ward and ask the important questions. \"Can a Vurdalak become a Verhen?\"","\"Yes, you obnoxious prick, or I wouldn’t be here.\" Salaark appeared out of thin air with Leegaain by her side. \"That baby carries a drop of my blood. It’s just one, but I could feel it all the way to the Blood Desert.\"","Her glare brought the Redcap and every other elder witnessing or listening to the conversation to their knees.","\"Interrupt any of us again with your disgusting comments, and it will be the last thing you ever do!\" She turned to Lith, her furious expression becoming sweet and caring. \"Thank you so much, Featherling.","\"I know how much you despise your brother and how much this must have cost you. Yet I want you to know that even though my spite for Meln is no less than yours, I still mourn my blood he possessed.","\"Thanks to you, Featherling, that blood is no longer lost. The potential that your revolting brother murdered, you brought it back to life. Back to me.\" Salaark cried softly.","\"It’s just one drop of blood, a potential that might not manifest itself for many generations, but it exists only thanks to you, Featherling. For that, you have my eternal gratitude.\"","\"And mine.\" Leegaain nodded, offering his hand to Lith. \"The star that your brother snuffed out now twinkles in my mind again, Lith. It’s just a tiny, flickering light, but still a light in the emptiness of space.","\"If you ever find a way to teach others how to conjure the Dread Flames, I will make you the next Father of Fire personally and give you anything you want in exchange for that knowledge. Before you ask, I mean it.","\"No matter how absurd your request might be, it would still be a small price to pay to ensure that my bloodline is safe and no corruption can taint it.\"","\"I’m going to take your word on that.\" Lith felt weak, and Leegaain conjured a chair for him to sit in and handed him one of his best tonics. \"I’d love to accept your proposal, but I have no idea if teaching Dread Flames is possible.","\"Even Tista never managed to do it.\"","\"Don’t worry, there’s no rush.\" The Father of All Dragons shook his head. \"If the time comes, however, my offer will always stand.\"","\"I don’t know how to thank you, Verhen.\" Althika said. \"I know it’s not much, but I’d like you to name my baby.\"","’Thank Bohr she doesn’t want to name him after me!’ Lith inwardly sighed in relief.","Solus wanted to scold him for dragging an innocent baby into his grudge with Orpal, but she remained silent, proud of what he had done.","\"I know it’s a weird name, but I would love it if you called him Erik.\" Lith said, scratching his head in embarrassment.","\"Don’t you mean Erlik?\" Salaark found it weird that Lith wanted to name a baby after the insane Treant-Draugr who had almost killed him, but his name at least made sense.","\"Or maybe Erkin\" Leegaain chimed in. \"Like the legendary hero of the Empire.\"","\"No, just Erik.\" Lith shook his head. \"If you share their misgivings, Althika, feel free to alter the name like you see fit. I don’t want your child to be mocked all his life because of me. He already has enough of that in store for him because of Meln.\"","\"With all due respect, I’ll call him Erkin.\" The Dryad blushed a bit. \"It contains all the letters of the name of your choice and will give my son someone to look up to.\"","\"Fine by me.\" Lith raised his hands, inwardly admitting that an English name on Mogar would have sounded out of place. \"That said, after all we’ve seen and heard, I don’t know if I can leave you in the hands of the Redleaf clan.","\"You carry Erkin Verhen in your womb, and your so-called family has already demonstrated they only care about what he can do for them. I’m afraid that if you stay here, they might subject your son to experiments to Awaken him and then turn him into a Demon.","\"It would give the Redleaf Clan the access to a Divine Beast bloodline they always wanted and even a bargaining chip with the Human Council. If the baby develops an Indech side like me, your clan can sell or rent him to let the humans study the secrets of their evolution.\"","\"Gods, no!\" Althika wrapped her arms around her swollen belly to protect it.","All the joy and hope she felt until a moment ago were gone, replaced by fear and horror. Luckily for her, the gods stood right by her side and seemed to like those potential scenarios as much as she did."]},{"number":4516,"title":"Chapter 4516 One Drop (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"For this reason, I offer you hospitality, Althika.\" Lith continued. \"You’d be my honored guest at the Mansion until the baby is born. After that, we’ll have to find you a different arrangement.","\"You have my word that whatever you decide, you’ll have my full support and I won’t let anyone interfere with your plans.\"","\"You and me both, Hatchling.\" Leegaain snorted, releasing thick puffs of black smoke from his nose. \"I won’t let a bunch of arrogant Fae and plant folk abuse the little miracle that Erkin is.","\"If they snuff out his flame, I’ll snuff out theirs. I will not rest until everyone involved is reduced to a pile of ashes attached to just enough flesh to beg for a mercy they won’t receive!\"","\"Order and Chaos, you’re so sexy when you act all romantic.\" Salaark said, blushing like a maiden.","How Leegaain’s oath to bring searing death and agony to the Redleaf clan could be considered sweet talk was a mystery that no one wanted to solve.","\"Also, you’d better not forget about me, you worthless pieces of rotten wood.\" The Overlord’s smile turned upside down as she stared right into the surveillance mirrors. \"Touch that child, and I’ll make you sworn enemies of my Nest. This I vow.","\"As for you, sweetie, you can come to the Desert with me, if you want.\" Salaark moved to Althika’s bedside and took her hand. \"Don’t get me wrong. Lith is a perfect host and a great cook, but his life is messy and dangerous.","\"Nobody would hurt you in my house, instead, and no harm can befall those who carry my blood under my roof.\"","\"I offer my hospitality as well, but in your shoes, I’d accept Salaark’s proposal.\" Leegaain said. \"You might feel lonely in my home since there’s only me most of the time, while despite all his power, Lith is just a Divine Beast.","\"In the Desert, instead, you’d be surrounded by people and protected by the most powerful Guardian on Mogar.\"","\"Stop it.\" Salaark giggled like a little girl. \"You’re making me blush.\"","\"I agree with Leg- Grandpa.\" Lith said. \"Meln might try to target you if he learns of what happened here, and I can’t always be there to protect you. Moreover, you’d always be one Gate away from my Mansion and family.\"","\"I accept your offer, Overlord Salaark. Please, protect my baby.\" Althika tried to stand up despite her exhaustion, but her legs failed her.","Baba Yaga had to support her and conjure a floating chair for her with Light Mastery.","\"No need for formalities, child. Salaark is enough.\" The Overlord pointed her finger at the Dryad’s forehead and released a spark of light. \"You’re under my aegis now, and any enemy of yours is mine until our agreement is rescinded.\"","\"Excellent.\" Lith took a deep breath to test his strength, discovering it had fully recovered. \"As for you, Lotho, and you members of the Redleaf clan, I have a message I want you to relay to the rest of your kin.","\"I know Meln. He would never be content with just one woman. There must be at least a handful of other Althikas out there.\"","\"You’re right.\" The Dryad nodded. \"There were four more women with me, and they all got pregnant with Meln’s baby. Three of them were plant folk and Fae. I know their names, but not their clans. We consider each other rivals and didn’t talk much.\"","\"This is my message.\" Lith said. \"If you need my help saving the babies, call for me, and I’ll come. Keep the babies a secret, or let the Vurdalak’s curse take its course, and I’ll become your sworn enemy.","\"I’ll find and kill anyone who has sacrificed the infants for their own gain, and I won’t have any mercy for their mothers if, unlike Althika, they gave in to their lowest impulses. The Vurdalak bloodline is a disease that must be cleansed.","\"How I must do it and how many people will have to die for it is up to you. Did I make myself clear?\"","The Guardians and Baba Yaga released their pressure, and the Fae replied, \"Crystal.\"","\"Then we have no reason to stay here any longer. We’ll take our leave. Lady Yaga?\" Lith asked, and the Crone delivered, Warping him and Althika to Bloodhaven.","The Crone didn’t move from the medical ward, holding Naphila’s flower in her palm and wondering what to do.","\"I’m really tempted to kill you and the rest of your people for what you planned to do to Lith, Naphila.\" She said.","\"What about me? They wanted to kill me as well!\" Lotho snarled.","\"I don’t care.\" The Crone shrugged. \"You’ve let yourself be manipulated like a seedling and brought us here. You deserve everything that happens to you, Lotho. On the other hand, I don’t want to taint this auspicious day with blood.","\"Scum like you aren’t worth my time.\" Baba Yaga tossed the flower at the Plant Representative, and he caught it. \"There. Now you have control over her and the arrays of this place.","\"I hear you plants are petty, vengeful, and cruel. I hope you fit the bill. Whatever you do, record everything and deliver the footage to Lith. I’ll collect it and save it for a day I’m sad and in need of a good laugh.\"","She disappeared as well, leaving no witness to whatever Lotho decided to do to erase the humiliation Naphila and her elders had put him through.","\"Petty, vengeful, and cruel?\" Lotho quoted Baba Yaga. \"She had no idea what an understatement that is. You, instead, my dear Naphila, know better. Now, imagine our roles were reversed, and you were the one holding my Root.","\"Imagine what you would do in my shoes. I’ll give you five minutes. After that, I promise you that whatever you pictured, I’ll do much worse to you.\"","***","\"Is this really a mage tower?\" Althika found herself in a comfortable bed in a room where the floor had been replaced by extraordinarily fertile soil. \"It looks so ordinary.\"","\"Appearances can be deceiving, child.\" Salaark replied. \"This is indeed Yaga’s tower, Bloodhaven. Feel free to feed off the ground. You and Erkin underwent a major procedure and need to eat to recover your strength.\"","The Dryad had started feeding when Baba Yaga joined them.","\"I’ve done everything I had to. Are you ready to leave, Lith?\" Solus’ ring moved back on his finger, and Starforge joined her a moment later.","\"Yes. Bring us to the Verhen Mansion, please.\" Lith nodded. \"Althika, there’s someone I want you to meet before you go to the Desert. Grandma, Grandpa, I’ll need your help to introduce her to the adults of my family.\"","\"You can count on me, Hatchling.\" Leegaain stared at the Dryad’s womb with the loving gaze of a grandfather eager to meet the newest member of the family. \"Anything else?\"","\"Actually, yes.\" Lith sighed. \"Althika, do you mind if we leave you alone for a second? There’s something I need to-\"","Lith turned to the Dryad and noticed she had fallen into a deep sleep. Between the pain, the fear, and the exhaustion from the multiple procedures on her life force, Althika had held on for so long only thanks to the adrenaline rush.","As soon as she felt safe and protected inside Bloodhaven and surrounded by Guardians, her body gave out."]},{"number":4517,"title":"Chapter 4517 Diminished (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"I’d rather we stay by Althika’s side.\" Baba Yaga Hushed the Dryad to ensure nothing would disturb her rest. \"She’s not going to listen to a word anyway.\"","\"I’m okay with that. Solus, do you mind joining us?\"","\"What’s the matter?\" She came out of the stone ring.","\"I need to share a few things with you guys. With all of you.\" Lith offered his hands, and the others formed a circle to complete the mind link.","He showed them everything that had happened from his point of view. He started with the voices in his head, then shared what he had seen with Spirit Vision and learned from it, to his combined use of Dread and Scourge Flames.","\"Order and Chaos, I’d call the Vurdalak’s life force an abomination, but that would be demeaning to all Abominations and even Eldritches!\" Salaark snarled. \"That’s a monstrosity, Yaga.","\"Something not even the worst Forbidden Magic I’ve ever encountered ever did. How is that possible?\"","\"I believe it’s thanks to the combination of Meln’s multiple bloodlines and the nigh-immortality Night bestows upon him.\" The Crone shapeshifted into her Mother form. \"Without Meln, Night’s experiment would’ve failed, yet without her, he wouldn’t have survived the procedure.","\"As you called it, Salaark, it’s a monstrosity born out of opportunity and unusual circumstances.\"","\"That’s not what I wanted to show you, though.\" Lith replied. \"It was just the context you needed to understand this.\"","He replayed how he had needed the Scourge Flames to purge Orpal’s essence and Dread Flames to cleanse the Vurdalak life force.","\"As I see it, Scourge Flames are the equivalent of darkness magic for a healer. They can only destroy, true, but they are also the only means you have to get rid of a parasite.","\"Meln’s essence was so intertwined with Althika’s life force that the Dread Flames alone couldn’t destroy one without killing the other. Scourge Flames, instead, ignited only Meln’s essence. No matter where it moved or how deep it hid.","\"The Scourge Flames never lost track of their target. I limited their movement with Dread Flames because I didn’t want the parasite to ravage Althika’s body in its futile attempts to escape, but Scourge Flames could have done it on their own.\"","\"Following your parallel, Dread Flames are healing magic, instead.\" Leegaain nodded. \"They clean the wound, sew it closed, and remove the infection, but their effect depends on the patient fighting the infection.","\"Like when you cleansed Raum’s lab. The world energy and the lingering souls were struggling to get free, and the Dread Flames cleansed them. If they had been infected with a malignant soul that spread and fueled the corruption, you would have needed Scourge Flames to burn the malignant soul first.\"","\"Exactly.\" Lith nodded. \"I wanted to show this to you, Grandpa, because you’re the greatest expert on Origin Flames I know.\"","\"What about me?\" Salaark grunted.","\"No offense, Grandma, but I’ve never heard anything about you having anything close to a Father of Fire. As far as I know, the only purification you deal with is the treatment of the ingredients for your Forgemastery.","\"Not a single Phoenix ever offered to teach me anything, whereas Valtak came to me and explained that he just upheld the tradition Grandpa established.\"","\"Point taken.\" She sighed.","\"I wanted to share everything also with you and Yaga because I hope you can help me understand my abilities so that if you ever need them, I can help you.\"","\"That’s a lovely thought, child.\" The Mother gave him a perfect curtsy. \"I’ll do what I can.\"","\"And so will I, Featherling.\" Salaark ruffled his hair. \"I’m proud of you. You may have inherited the elements of destruction from us, but you employ them to rid Mogar of what can’t be saved or doesn’t want to be saved.\"","’Thanks for being close to me yet giving me my space, Solus.’ Lith said via the mind link. ’I didn’t know how much I needed to make that decision on my own until I did.’","’Don’t mention it.’ She replied, giving him the telepathic equivalent of a hug. ’Fate sure has a twisted sense of humor. The very day you decided to forgive Trion, you also had to face a similar decision regarding Meln’s son.’","’Do you think this might be Mogar’s doing?’ Lith went full paranoia, but even he couldn’t see a connection between the two events.","’Mogar doesn’t care about something this small.’ Solus pondered. ’Besides, that would require her to have somehow manipulated all the events since the day Meln attacked Bornar. That’s a lot of work, and for what?","’Mogar doesn’t get anything out of this, and there were too many factors involved. Althika might have made a different decision, and so could you. There were infinite possible outcomes. Too many to control them all.","’Also, you are the one who made the final decision. Did you feel any external influence?’","’I wish.’ Lith inwardly sighed. ’I’ve never been so conflicted in my whole life. I wanted to ask your advice, Kami’s, and even Mom’s, but I knew the responsibility of everything that came next was going to be mine.","’Putting that burden on your shoulders would have been cruel. I was alone, Solus. More than I’ve ever been since the day we met.’","’This settles it, then.’ She nodded. ’ Back to the problem. Assuming that we can explain everything properly to the grown-ups and things don’t blow up in our faces, what do we tell the kids?’","’That’s one decision I’m glad that I don’t have to take alone.’ Lith replied. ’Grandma and Grandpa will help us, and so will our parents. Also, if you are listening to this, Mogar, feel free to chime in. I can use an extra hand.’","Only silence ensued. Mogar was aware of every speck of dust on its surface. The planet knew where it had originated, how it had reached its current position, and where it would probably land next.","Yet it didn’t alter even such a trivial outcome. Even producing a gust of wind would have triggered a domino effect that would have affected many other events until lives were lost.","So Mogar kept spinning like usual, hoping that someone else would stop the speck of dust and prevent the next domino tile from falling.","***","Jiera Continent, Maneka Region, fortress of Nareka, at the same time.","A piercing pain woke the Dead King from his peaceful slumber. His blood seemed to have burst into flames, and not the corrupted flames that bestowed power and strength upon him. It was real, scorching fire that burned everything in its path.","’What’s wrong with me? What’s happening?’ Meln used his breathing technique, Birthright, to check on his body, and when he found nothing wrong, he stirred Night awake.","’You’re fine, and so am I.’ She replied. ’If anything bad were happening, my regenerative enchantments would have kicked in, and I would know. Nothing is wrong, and our breathing techniques just confirmed it.’","’Then why- Gods!’ Orpal clenched his chest as the pain rose in intensity, as if someone had stabbed him with a sword and twisted it in the wound before pulling it out.","He felt as if he had a gaping, bleeding hole in his body, yet on the surface everything looked fine."]},{"number":4518,"title":"Chapter 4518 Diminished (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Lith had just finished cleansing Meln’s essence from Althika’s body, killing the extension of the Dead King’s consciousness he wasn’t aware he had spawned.","’I don’t know.’ Night answered the incomplete question. ’Also, you were right. Something is wrong with you. Your aura just dimmed for no apparent reason. Let’s call Jorl!’","The Storm Griffon was an accomplished Light Master and the best Healer among the Upyrs. He gladly answered the call, eager to learn more about the Dead King’s life force and maybe discover an easy way to kill or restrain him.","\"I agree with Night. Something is wrong with you, but it’s nothing any of my spells can detect. Even my breathing technique says you’re fine. This doesn’t make any sense.\"","\"I called you for help, not-\" Orpal’s voice broke into a scream of pain that rose in intensity and became shriller as Lith dismantled Erkin’s Vurdalak life force.","The Dead King felt every incision and cauterization. He experienced the cleansing touch of the Dread Flames as they killed a part of the Vurdalak bloodline. When the procedure ended, both father and son were changed.","Orpal looked smaller and weaker. His entire being was diminished by the loss. The Dead King felt as if part of his soul had been burned alive, and he with it.","\"I’m going to kill the first person who tells me I’m fine; I don’t care who they are.\" He snarled, the intensity of his suffering taking Night and Jorl by surprise, but for completely different reasons.","The Horseman of Night too felt weaker, needing sheer willpower not to fall asleep again. Jorl, instead, hadn’t felt that well since the day Light Soul had stolen part of his Griffon life force.","The pain in his chest abated, and the Vurdalak side’s relentless attack on the Griffon life force ceased.","\"I’ll order Erion to reach his contacts for news.\" Jorl said. \"You’d better rest and stay out of sight. We can’t let our soldiers know of your condition. If anything else happens, don’t hesitate to contact me.\"","\"Thanks, Jorl.\" Orpal grunted. \"What if someone asks you where I am and what I’m doing?\"","\"I’ll tell them that you’ve gone out to pick up Jiera’s most gorgeous women for your harem, and they’ll believe it.\" The Storm Griffon replied.","\"I like how you think.\" The Dead King was still thanking the gods for having a reliable second-in-command when he fell asleep.","’Fuck!’ Jorl thought. ’Night is still awake, or I’d Sealed Space them to cut them off from Moonlight and bring them to the Black Throne while they are weakened.’","He turned around and left the room, bolting to meet the cursed tower as soon as he made sure he had covered his traces properly.","\"You did the right thing, apprentice.\" The Black Throne revised Jorl’s memories, studying Orpal’s life force and current condition. \"The Dead King’s affliction is neither physical or magical.","\"His life force and mana core are at full strength and ready to fight. Alone and without a plan, you had no chance against Night. The information you brought me is priceless and greatly increases our chances of victory and of healing you.","\"Enter the crystal tank, quick!\" The Black Throne Warped the Storm Griffon to his lab and operated on the contaminated life force in Jorl’s chest.","\"The Vurdalak fragment inside of you is as weakened and stunned as Orpal.\" The cursed tower said. \"This is a perfect chance to fine-tune your treatment.\"","The Black Throne used his Body Sculpting spell, Needlework, to restore the corrupted life force to its original state and stimulate the Griffon side to reclaim what it had lost to Light Soul.","Much to Jorl and the cursed tower’s surprise, the Vurdalak side offered almost no resistance, and the Griffon side fought it beak and talon. By the end of the procedure, the corrupted life force was permanently weakened, and the Griffon side had regained a millimeter of lost tissue.","It was a small, almost imperceptible victory, but a victory nonetheless. The pain in Jorl’s chest had sensibly diminished, and he could finally breathe easily again.","\"Don’t get your hopes up, apprentice.\" The Black Throne said. \"If the Dead King’s condition improves, yours will deteriorate. You’ll be in almost as much pain as before, so keep yourself ready to hide your illness.\"","\"Still, this is progress.\" Jorl nodded.","\"No, this is a breakthrough!\" The cursed tower laughed. \"Maybe the first of many. I’ll stop my travels for a while. If this happens again, I want you to collect as much information as you can and then rush to me.","\"We’ll use everything we learn to improve on your treatment and rid you of the Vurdalak, apprentice. Or rather, to keep it under control until Orpal is dead. Without him, his tissues should lose their semi-sentience.","\"Once that happens, you’ll take his place as the main Vurdalak and with my help, you’ll become the most powerful Divine Beast Mogar has ever seen!\"","***","Garlen Continent, Verhen Mansion.","Bloodhaven appeared in the keep, yet the end of the trip marked the start of Lith’s troubles.","\"Althika is still sleeping. This will make things easier, but not by much.\" Lith said. \"Solus, put Starforge in position. I’ll have everyone assemble while Grandma and Grandpa take the kids away.\"","The Guardians invited the children to play in an amusement park they conjured out of thin air. Even if the kids took each ride only once, Lith would have all the time he needed.","\"You’re making me worry, son.\" Raaz said once the Verhen family had been brought together, even at the cost of rudely dismissing their guests without a shred of explanation. \"What’s going on? Why all this secrecy?\"","\"I’m about to tell you something important, Dad, and even though the Ernas and Ryla are our good friends, they are not part of the family.\" Lith replied. \"They won’t take part in our decision until we’ve made it.","\"I don’t want you to feel peer-pressured into doing something you don’t want.\"","\"Okay, I’m still confused, but now I’m also worried to death.\" Raaz said. \"What’s going on, son? And this time explain yourself in a way that makes sense.\"","\"One moment.\" Lith conjured Trion and all the other Demons, but only allowed his older brother and Menadion to stay. \"You are family, Ripha, and have the right to weigh in on this.\"","\"Thanks?\" Menadion scratched her head in embarrassment.","\"Take my hands for a mind link, or this will take all day.\" Lith shared the details of his day from Lotho’s call to his return to the Mansion with his family, sparing them only the gruesome details of the procedure.","\"We are going to have a grandchild?\" It was the first time Elina said those words with pursed lips and blood draining from her face instead of a joyful expression. \"From Meln?\"","She looked at her husband, noticing he was frozen in horror. No one hated or despised Orpal more than Raaz. Being tortured by his disowned son had left deep mental and emotional scars that would haunt Lith’s father for the rest of his life.","The idea of having Orpal’s blood under his roof was more than he could take."]},{"number":4519,"title":"Chapter 4519 Lesson about Compassion (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Up to five grandchildren, actually.\" Lith replied. \"There are four more women out there pregnant with his children, and if they ask for my help, I’ll save them.\" A wave of his hand conjured hot tea and alcohol to spike it for everyone.","The Verhens sipped the liquor from the bottle and needed several minutes to recover from the emotional blow enough to speak, even Trion.","\"I can’t believe you offered Althika hospitality, Lil Bro.\" Tista’s hand trembled, making her cup clink against the saucer multiple times. \"I mean, it was nice of you, but-\"","\"Also insane!\" Rena snarled. \"Orpal- I mean, Meln is a murderous, deranged, perverted piece of shit, and you invited his bastard child into our home without even consulting us? Have you forgotten what he’s done to you?","\"To Aran and Leria? To Zin and her children? More importantly, have you forgotten what he did to Dad?\" She pointed at Raaz, making him flinch as if her finger were a poisoned blade.","\"I haven’t forgotten.\" Lith was surprised by how calm he was in the middle of the storm. \"This changes nothing. I will find Meln, and I will kill him in the most painful way I can. Yet we are not talking about him, but his child.","\"Blaming Erkin for his father’s crimes would be no different than pinning on Garrik the countless atrocities Glemos perpetrated on the people of Zelex. Or do you think that by saving him I also forgave his insane father for his crimes?\"","\"Yes, I mean, no. I mean, it’s not the same thing!\" Rena backed off, knowing how nonsensical she sounded.","\"Explain to me how.\" Lith crossed his arms. \"As I see it, the only difference between Erkin and Garrik is that you never met Glemos and were never personally affected by his actions. Garrik is a good kid, and you know it.","\"Erkin is not even born. There’s nothing you can accuse him of aside from being alive, but that would make everyone on this planet just as guilty.\"","A long, awkward silence befell the room. Lith’s reasoning was flawless, and the fact he had chosen the baby’s name carried great weight.","\"Lith has a point.\" Trion was terrified that anything he said might be misunderstood as him siding with Orpal like when they were kids, but he had to speak. \"Meln is a cancer on Mogar, but we can’t take it on his son.","\"I’m not saying we should hug Althika and welcome her to the family. We can never meet her, for all I care. Yet the baby will need help growing up, and we are the only ones who can give it to him.","\"If even Erkin’s family can barely tolerate his existence, imagine how the rest of Mogar will treat him.\"","\"I can sort of agree.\" Rena clenched her hands in frustration. \"Sort of. And mostly because if the little bastard becomes a Demon, people might study him to discover the weaknesses of our children.","\"The Dryad, however, is a different story. She’s nothing but a whore! She knew who Meln was, yet she searched for him, she seduced him, and got pregnant with his child! She’s nothing like Ryla. Ryla was born in Zelex and had no way out.","\"She believed Glemos to be a god and gave him a son because she was forced to. This Althika, instead, is an opportunistic, soulless monster just like Meln and deserves everything she gets!\"","\"I’m not even going to try to justify that.\" Lith raised his hands, conceding the point. \"Yet I’m asking you all to remember that she’s not a human. You can’t judge Althika by our standards more than you can blame Abominus and Onyx for eating those who try to harm Aran and Leria.\"","Everyone shuddered at those words. Witnessing the fluffy magical beasts the Verhens considered huge plushies murder and eat humans like cattle had been their first interspecies great cultural shock.","The Verhens considered the act revolting, but to the beasts it was the most natural thing. The only reason the Verhens eased into accepting the beasts’ feeding habits was that Abominus and Onyx only ate those they killed, and they killed only those who wanted to harm Aran and Leria.","Even the most compassionate among the Verhens felt no pity or empathy for such people and wished them the most gruesome death. Moreover, once the rumors about the fate of the assailants spread, the number of attempts on the kids had plummeted.","It made their parents even more grateful to the beasts and uncaring about the suffering of the criminals.","\"Moreover, as Naphila said, Althika underwent a drastic change after getting pregnant, just like it happened to Ryssa after she started dating Marth.\" Lith said. \"Seeing her today, you’d never believe what she did and how she behaved in the White Griffon’s forest.","\"Back then, she only cared about her sister, Lyta, and considered anyone else, even the young students, as either food or playthings. Ryssa changed because Marth showed her another way of living, while Althika grew to love her baby.","\"I want you to understand, Rena, that Erkin wasn’t human, but a Vurdalak. The corruption it brought should have reinforced Althika’s race impulse to prey on the weak, yet she fought with everything she had.","\"If she were as evil as you claim, why did she endure so much suffering when she could have just given in?\"","Elina’s and Rena’s focus shifted from the baby’s father to the events before the procedure that Lith had shown them. Althika’s pain and despair as she fought a losing battle to keep her baby safe struck many nerves, and it struck hard.","Both women had almost lost a child, and could walk more than one mile in the Dryad’s shoes.","’My body betrayed me just like Althika’s and killed Lith.’ Elina thought. ’I don’t know what I’d done if he didn’t come back on his own.’","’She may be a piece of shit, but at least she fought for Erkin as hard as I did for Falco.’ Rena shuddered; the parallel between the Strangler and Orpal’s influence hit too close to home.","\"Allow me to add one thing, Little Brother.\" Much to everyone’s surprise, Trion used a moniker, and Lith didn’t glare or sneer at him. \"I know that what Althika did is wrong. There is no changing that.","\"Yet as someone who made many mistakes, I need to ask. If you think redemption is impossible, if those marked as bad people can’t change, why let them live? Wouldn’t it be much better and faster to put them down?","\"I know I acted like an idiot all my life, but I like to think that maybe, just maybe, if I realized the error of my ways and found a way to make it up to you, you’d have forgiven me and let me back into your lives.","\"Without this thought, my existence as a Demon would be intolerable because it would mean you’ll never forgive me and you tolerate my presence only out of pity.\"","\"Don’t you say that!\" Elina jumped from her seat and rushed to hug the Demon. \"Don’t you ever say that, baby. Of course, we would have taken you back.\""]},{"number":4520,"title":"Chapter 4520 Lesson about Compassion (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Your mother is right, son.\" Raaz stood up and moved to Trion’s side. \"I can’t speak for the rest of the family, but I would have forgiven you. Maybe it would have taken me longer than Elina, but you can bet your shadow ass I would have welcomed you back in the family.\"","\"Don’t look at me, the jury is still out on that.\" Lith replied to those staring at him. \"But what Big Brother says makes sense, if one believes in forgiveness.\"","Lith returning the moniker without a shred of sarcasm or spite brooked no further doubt about the change in his relationship with Trion.","\"Fine.\" Rena sighed. \"After all, Althika didn’t hurt or endanger anyone but herself with her actions. We should at least get to know her before burning her at the stake.\"","\"Big sis!\" Tista was flabbergasted. \"Since when are you the violent one? That’s Lith’s thing!\"","\"Shut up! Rena snorted. \"Like it wasn’t already bad having to take lessons about compassion from Lith. You guys are making me feel like a monster.\"","Raaz hadn’t said much, but he had given the matter a lot of thought. Yet his mind and heart were still at odds with his rampaging trauma.","\"Please, be honest with me, Lith.\" He said. \"Is the baby...\"","Silence stretched for long seconds as Raaz mustered the strength to finish his sentence.","\"Really cured? Is there anything of Meln left in him?\"","\"I’m sorry, Dad.\" Lith replied. \"The baby’s genetic material is indeed half Meln and half Dryad. Nothing can change that.\"","He paused, letting those words sink in.","\"Yet Erkin is his own person. He’s no Vurdalak and carries no trace of either Meln or Night. He’s a baby no different from Dhiral or Leria. For what it’s worth, he has no conscience or morals yet, but he refused to feed on his mother.","\"He perceived the threat Althika posed to him, yet refused to fight her. In my book, this says a lot. The little fellow hasn’t even seen the light of day, but he’s already nothing like his father.\"","Raaz mulled over the memories of what he had seen and heard during the mind link for a few seconds before making up his mind.","\"I agree with you, son.\" Raaz nodded. \"If you don’t mind, I’d like to meet my grandchild. You guys stay here and-\"","\"I’m coming with you.\" Elina said.","\"Same.\" Trion nodded. \"In a world of people who’ll hate Erkin for his blood, he needs someone like me to teach him how not to become a total fool.\"","\"Gods, I can’t believe I’m saying this, but I’m coming too.\" Tista sighed. \"I hate Meln, but Erkin is a Demon, and Demons stick together.\"","\"Kami, Senton, this leaves just us.\" Rena pinched her nose in frustration.","\"Who’s us?\" Kamila asked. \"I didn’t say anything because I know how hard this is on every one of you, but I’ve made up my mind since Lith shared his inner struggle with us. He named Erkin and offered him hospitality. That’s more than enough for me.\"","Kamila and Solus were the only ones aware of Lith’s first life and also the only ones he had shared the entire procedure with. They knew about Carl and what the name Erik meant to Lith.","\"Please, Dear, don’t tell me that the only reason you’re still sitting is that you don’t want to leave me alone.\" Rena said to her husband.","\"I’ll remain silent, then.\" He gave her a warm smile and held her hand.","\"Thanks.\" Rena stood up, still feeling unsteady on her feet and in her beliefs. \"What are we going to say to the children? What do we do if they ask us who the father of their cousin is?\"","\"Aran and Leria are old enough to understand the truth, if we explain it to them clearly.\" Lith said. \"As for the triplets, let’s keep things simple. We’ll tell them Althika is Trion’s girlfriend and the baby is his.\"","\"What?\" The entire family said in unison.","\"It’s the simplest and most practical solution.\" Lith shrugged. \"The triplets still believe that a child is born when a mom and a dad share a special hug that makes the mom bloat until the baby pops out by miracle.","\"Moreover, Falco and his siblings have no idea how my Demons work, and Trion can still hug people. As for the toddlers, they have no concept of baby-making at all. We just point them at an alleged father, and they’ll buy it.\"","\"I’m not saying you’re wrong, little brother, just that I don’t like your idea.\" Trion snorted.","\"Then how do we explain our blood ties with Althika’s baby?\" Lith replied. \"Do you want to tell the children that Dad or I are the father?\"","\"Gods, no!\" Trion shuddered at the idea. \"Maybe...\"","His mind went blank, and no matter how much he pondered the issue, he couldn’t find a valid alternative to Lith’s solution.","\"Let’s go with your idea, then.\" Trion sighed. \"A bit of embarrassment is worth sparing that poor child from being hated by the rest of our little ones. Where is Althika?\"","\"Inside my tower, resting.\" Baba Yaga said. \"If it makes you feel better, she never left her room or set foot in the Mansion. Neither she nor her baby entered your home at any moment.\"","Raaz gritted his teeth at the allegation, but was secretly relieved at the news. And he wasn’t the only one. Despite their words and rational thoughts, most of the Verhens found the idea of Orpal’s blood violating the sanctity of their home revolting.","’Maybe things will change once I get to know Althika and the baby, but right now the best intentions in the world can’t stop me from seeing her like Meln’s whore and the baby as his accursed spawn.’ Raaz thought.","\"Do you want to visit her, or do you want me to move her to the Blood Desert right away?\" Baba Yaga asked.","\"I think we should meet her at least once.\" Raaz said, color draining from his face. \"If we’re going to be her family, we can’t send her away without even introducing ourselves.\"","\"That’s thoughtful of you, dear.\" Elina said, yet the word her tone conveyed was, brave. \"I agree with you.\"","The Verhens approved Raaz’s suggestion one after the other, until the decision was unanimous.","\"There’s no point in delaying the inevitable.\" Raaz swallowed hard. \"Let’s do it now and get it out of the way. Can you please bring us to her, Yaga?\"","’Dad is making it sound more like a dentist appointment than a family reunion, but this is terrific progress from him.’ Lith thought.","\"No problem.\" A wave of the Mother’s hand Warped everyone inside Bloodhaven, but in an antechamber outside Althika’s room. \"She’s behind that door. Take your time to prepare yourself if you need.","\"Also, if it’s of any help, she’s still sleeping. You don’t have to worry about losing your composure. I can wake her up after you’ve gotten used to her presence.\"","\"For the gods’ sake, this is ridiculous!\" Raaz snarled. \"We are taking so many precautions that one would think we’re about to meet a ferocious Dragon instead of the mother of my grandchild. Even worse, we have Dragons as guests for breakfast, lunch, and dinner!\""]},{"number":4521,"title":"Chapter 4521 Make it Better (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Raaz opened the door and stepped inside just to stop abruptly as if someone had slapped him in the face. The room was decorated with modest wooden furniture, and the woman sleeping in the bed at the center of the room was simply lovely.","Althika’s light green skin didn’t diminish the beauty of her features one bit. Quite the contrary, it brought out the red of her flaming hair. She looked peaceful, like a maiden from a fairy tale waiting for her mage charming to wake her up from a cursed slumber, not like a monster carrying another monster in her womb.","\"Well, at least she’s pretty.\" Rena tried to find something positive in that situation, but her words sounded hollow even to her.","\"Don’t worry, dear.\" Elina touched Raaz’s shoulder just to see him flinch. \"Think of her as Ryssa. They are both Dryads and come here as friends.\"","\"Thanks.\" Raaz nodded, his face pale and clammy.","He took one painful step after the other until he was at Althika’s bedside, his family right behind you. Only once he was close enough to the object of his fears to see her chest slowly heave when she breathed did the Guardians appear.","Salaark and Leegaain took position at the right and left of the bed respectively, spreading a soothing aura that seemed to lift a heavy burden from everyone’s shoulders.","\"Thank you, Featherlings.\" The Overlord said. \"I know how hard this must be for you.\"","\"Despite his origins, the baby is still of our blood.\" Leegaain said. \"We’ll do everything we can to make this as easy as possible for you.\"","\"Great, now everybody, step back.\" The Mother said. \"I don’t want Althika to wake up and find herself surrounded by strangers.\"","She shapeshifted back into her Crone form as she gently roused the Dryad from her sleep.","\"Wake up, child. I need to know how you feel.\"","\"I’m dead tired, and my body hurts in places I didn’t think they could, but aside from that, I feel great.\" Lith’s Dread Flames had purified Althika’s life force, leaving shallow yet extensive burn wounds that only time could heal. \"After days of pain and hunger, I feel r-\"","The words died in her mouth when she noticed Lith and the rest of the Verhens standing just a few meters away. The Dryad yelped in fear, wrapping herself in the blanket and squeezing Baba Yaga’s hand.","’She’s scared of us as much as I’m scared of her.’ Raaz couldn’t help but inwardly smile at the absurdity of the situation.","\"Don’t worry, child. These people are our friends.\" The Crone smiled at Althika while caressing her hand to reassure her. \"Allow me to introduce the Verhens to you. They are Erkin’s family, and one day they might become your family as well.\"","The introductions were awkward and tense, as if both parties were undergoing a job interview they desperately needed to pass. Even with the Guardians present, the tension in the room was palpable.","Althika avoided mentioning Orpal and the circumstances of Erkin’s conception, just like the Verhens avoided any topic that might lead to talk about the Dryad’s past.","\"Can I please take a look at Erkin?\" Elina decided to break the ice the only way she knew. \"I’m Awakened as well, but I’m not good with healing magic. I can’t check on your baby without Invigoration.\"","\"Sure.\" Althika swallowed hard, letting go of the blanket with the reluctance of a soldier dropping her shield during a battle.","Elina placed her hand on the Dryad’s womb, and both women shuddered at the physical contact. Althika had nothing against the Verhens, but she felt their reproach for her actions and spite for the father of her child.","’I can’t blame the Verhens for being so cold.’ She thought as Elina’s mana flowed through her. ’If I could turn back time, I would knock some sense into myself with an Adamant mace.’","\"Gods.\" Elina gasped, making everyone flinch. \"He’s perfect.\"","Contrary to her expectations, the baby didn’t have his father’s deranged eyes or cruel smile. Erkin was a perfectly normal baby, and recoiled in fear at the touch of Elina’s mana.","After everything he and his mother had endured that day, the unborn child feared that any external influence would bring more pain.","\"I’m sorry.\" Elina jolted back, warm tears streaking down her eyes. \"I didn’t mean to scare you.\"","\"What are you talking about?\" Althika asked in confusion.","\"What happened, Mom?\" Tista rushed to her side. \"Are you alright?\"","\"I am, sweetie, but Erkin is not.\" Elina sniffled. \"He was still a Divine Beast during the procedure, and I’m afraid that the first memory he has of this world is of suffering. He has yet to be born, yet he’s terrified of everything. He thinks we want to hurt him.\"","Those words hit everyone like a punch to the gut, especially Lith. They hated Orpal, but the thought that a small baby might consider them cruel monsters was too much to take.","’I did what I did to help him, but Erkin is too young to understand that.’ Lith clenched his hands so hard that his knuckles popped. ’To him I must be no better than Meln.’","Not to scare the baby further, the rest of the Verhens asked Elina to share her scan via a mind link. The images were vivid enough to give Raaz goosebumps and make him feel terrible when he witnessed Erkin quiver in the womb at the slightest touch of Elina’s breathing technique.","’He’s like me.’ Raaz thought. ’We both had to endure a world of pain because of Meln, cursed be his name. This poor boy almost killed his own mother due to the Vurdalak accursed bloodline.","’If Erkin remembers any of that, his life will be a nightmare for many years to come, even if the rest of Mogar treats him like a prince.’","\"I’m sorry, my child. I’m so sorry. This is all my fault.\" Althika sniffled after Elina shared her memories with the Dryad. \"I caused everyone so much pain. You can’t even meet your family because of me.\"","\"You went through a lot today.\" The Crone patted the Dryad’s back and offered her a handkerchief. \"We’ll continue this tomorrow, after you and Erkin have a bit more rest.\"","\"Continue?\" Althika echoed in confusion.","\"Yes, child.\" Baba Yaga nodded. \"The only way Erkin can learn the world is not just a cruel place is by experience. He needs to feel the touch of people who aren’t his mother and realize not everyone is out to hurt him.","\"I suggest letting one person use their breathing technique on you every day until things get better. It will help your child and his family to get closer over time.\"","Althika and the Verhens didn’t like the idea, but realized the problem wouldn’t get any better just by pretending it didn’t exist. In a few months, the baby would be born, and then Erkin would see their tense grimaces.","Baba Yaga moved Bloodhaven to the Desert, and the Verhens sighed in relief, but only until they racked their brains to break the news of Erkin’s existence to Aran and Leria without scaring them.","\"We have a cousin? Is Auntie Tista expecting a baby?\" Aran asked."]},{"number":4522,"title":"Chapter 4522 Make it Better (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"No!\" Tista blushed up to her ears. \"Why does everyone always think of me when we talk about children?\"","\"Because you’re the only one without one, Auntie.\" Leria replied. \"Mom?\"","\"No, it’s not me either.\" Rena cleared her throat in embarrassment. \"We’ll continue this conversation later.\"","The following day, the Verhens went to the Blood Desert to visit Althika without the children. Raaz decided he would check on the baby next and overcome his irrational fear of Erkin.","\"How are you doing today, Althika?\" He asked, his lips twitching often as he gave her a tense smile that almost resembled a feverish grin.","\"I’m still very tired, Mister Verhen.\" The Dryad needed Baba Yaga’s hand and heavy blankets to face her friendly opponents. \"No matter how long I sleep, I feel exhausted, and my entire body aches as if someone has just finished beating me up.\"","\"I’m sorry to hear.\" Raaz said, and much to his surprise, he was sincere. \"How is our little Erkin?\"","Using the name Lith had given the baby made him appear more human and less monstrous to Raaz’s imagination.","\"His condition is much better than when he was a Vurdalak.\" Althika smiled only when talking about her son. \"Erkin’s not tormented by his father’s madness anymore, and he’s happy all the time now. Yet he too feels weak and aches.\"","\"That’s normal.\" The Crone said. \"You two underwent a procedure of unprecedented magnitude. Your life forces need time to recover and heal from the scars left by Lith’s Dread Flames.\"","\"She’s right child.\" Salaark nodded. \"I’d gladly help you, but I have no idea how the Dread Flames work or how your life forces survived the destruction of the Upyr and Vurdalak side.","\"All I can tell you is that you and Erkin are fine, and on the way to a speedy recovery. Any clumsy meddling is likely to make things worse rather than better.\"","\"About that.\" Lith said, drawing attention to him. \"Maybe I know someone who can help. I’ll be right back.\"","He Warped out of the room and returned a second later, holding Valeron the Second in his arms.","\"Val, this lady is Althika, and she carries your cousin Erkin in her belly. Say hi to her.\" Lith said.","\"Hi, Auntie Alt... Alkt....\"","\"Call me Allie, sweetie.\" The Dryad chuckled at how cute he looked as he tried to say her name.","\"I’m sorry.\" Valeron blushed a bit. \"I’m not good with difficult words.\"","\"Nonsense, you’re doing great.\" Lith moved the baby boy closer to the Dryad, and she caressed his hair. \"You’re very smart for a boy your age.\"","\"Thanks, Auntie.\" Valeron smiled at the compliment.","\"Val, your auntie and cousin are recovering from a bad illness. Is there anything you can do to help them?\" Lith asked Althika’s permission to let the boy touch her, and she nodded.","\"I don’t know, Dad, but I can try.\" Valeron held the Dryad’s hand and shuddered.","He felt her pain, the open wounds in her life force left by the destruction of Orpal’s fragment and her Upyr side, and the imbalance the Vurdalak blood had wrought upon her.","Erkin fared even worse. Lith had restored his original life forces, but they were all weak, burned, and scarred. The Dread Flames had cauterized the cuts to perfection, but that didn’t make them any less tender or sore.","He listened to the melody of their life forces, finding no discordant note. Val then used Life Score to read mother’s and son’s symphonies, finding that every note was right, just a bit out of place. They would move into their right position once the life forces healed, if they healed completely.","\"You’re okay, Auntie.\" Valeron said. \"You and Eky are okay.\"","\"Thanks, sweetheart.\" Althika would have taken his words as just baby talk if not for how serious everyone else was. \"I needed good news.\"","\"I can make you better, though.\" Valeron looked at her with his big, silver eyes. \"Can I?\"","The question took the Dryad by surprise, and she looked at her hosts before answering.","\"Val’s not lying.\" Leegaain said. \"The choice is up to you.\"","\"I have no idea what’s going on, but I can assure you’re safe under my roof.\" Salaark said. \"No ill will befall you or Erkin here.\"","\"Can you really make my son better?\" Althika asked, and Valeron nodded. \"Then, please help him out.\"","\"Thanks, Auntie!\" The baby boy lit up with joy and shapeshifted into his Bahamut form. \"I promise this won’t hurt a bit.\"","\"What won’t- Gods!\" Valeron the Second infused himself with his Life Maelstrom, and a thin layer of Life Flames wreathed his body.","\"Don’t worry, Auntie. They don’t burn unless I ask them to. See?\" Valeron touched his clothes and the bedsheets, yet the golden flames didn’t spread or blacken anything.","Althika tentatively placed her hand on the Bahamut’s muzzle, finding it pleasantly warm. Instead of burning her fingers, the Life Flames washed her pain away as if a balm were being applied to her skin.","\"I trust you, Val.\" She nodded. \"Go on.\"","The small Bahamut breathed a gentle stream of golden flames that wrapped themselves around the Dryad, covering her from head to toe. They slowly seeped under her skin, burning the scars, wounds, and the pain, converting them into pure energy that filled the gaps in Althika’s life force.","Once Valeron was done with her, he moved on to Erkin. His Life Flames lapped at the burn scars in the baby’s life forces and nurtured them back to health. The golden fire wrapped the human, Dryad, and the Divine Beast sides, igniting them with inner light that shone brighter than the sum of its single parts.","Yet no matter how strongly the Life Flames burned, mother and child experienced only the warmth of a tender embrace.","\"I’m sorry, Auntie.\" Valeron reverted to his human form, panting. \"I’m too weak. I couldn’t do it. I’m...\"","He slumped asleep in Lith’s arms the moment he took Valeron off the bed.","\"Why did he apologize?\" Althika asked. \"I didn’t feel any discomfort, and now I’m better than-\"","A pillar of orange light emerged from her body, and another descended from the sky as Mogar assisted the Dryad in her evolution into a Titania. Althika’s vines dug deep into the fertile soil of Salaark’s oasis, extracting large amounts of nutrients and water.","It was no different from how a plant folk regenerated their wounds, except that new mass formed and the old one grew in size and power. The Dryad underwent a complete metamorphosis in a handful of seconds.","The transformation was so smooth and natural that no one had any issue recognizing Althika in the much taller and beautiful redhead in front of them. It was also the reason no one noticed Tyris’ arrival.","\"What? How?\" The Titania’s utter disbelief didn’t stop her from checking on her son before examining her new body.","Erkin was better than fine. His life force shone bright and healthy, with no traces of his healing wounds.","\"It seems the Vurdalak blood was the reason you failed to evolve upon reaching the blue core, child.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"The invasion of the Upyr life force had infected your Dryad side and stopped its natural development.\""]},{"number":4523,"title":"Chapter 4523 Coveted Bloodline (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Lith’s treatment removed the Upyr side, but your body couldn’t evolve until it recovered from the scars left by the procedure. Once Val healed them, nature ran its course.\" Baba Yaga said.","\"Thank the gods!\" After ensuring that Erkin was fine, Althika sighed in relief. \"I was afraid I would have remained stuck as a Dryad for the rest of my life as penance for my stupidity.\"","\"Don’t thank us, child.\" Tyris said, making everyone flinch when they heard her voice and finally noticed she had joined them. \"We did nothing. Your condition was beyond us. It’s Lith and my little Val you have to thank.\"","\"Thank you, Lith.\" The Titania beamed with joy. \"Thank you... Val?\"","The baby boy was deep asleep, clinging to Lith with all his strength.","\"I’ll thank him on your behalf when he wakes up.\" Lith was as surprised as anyone else, but he didn’t miss that there was something off with the Guardians.","’Tyris never arrives uninvited, especially on someone else’s turf.’ He thought. ’Moreover, speeding up Althika’s recovery can’t be the reason the three Guardians of Garlen are so shocked.’","Leegaain, Salaark, and Tyris didn’t bother hiding their feelings, and they looked more surprised at the Dryad’s sudden evolution than the Verhens even though they had lived countless millennia longer.","\"I’d say this was enough excitement for today, Althika. You and Erkin need rest.\" Lith said.","\"Indeed.\" The Titania yawned. \"I feel even more tired than before. I’m sorry for sending you away so soon after barely exchanging a few words. I hope we’ll spend more time together tomorrow.\"","She drifted into a peaceful slumber the moment she closed her eyes.","A snap of Lith’s fingers Warped everyone out of the room and inside the tower.","\"Okay, what was that?\" He asked. \"You know that Val inherited his father’s affinity for life forces and that his Life Flames can heal people. He already used them on Valtak, yet you didn’t seem to care much back then. What’s so different now?\"","\"You’re right, Featherling-\"","\"Not so fast, young sparrow!\" Tyris snorted, her beautiful features twisted in annoyance. \"Val is my grandchild, so I’ll do the honors.\"","\"Fine.\" The Overlord crossed her arms and pouted.","\"As Salaark was saying, Lith, you’re right.\" Tyris said, reverting to her usual, lovely countenance. \"The healing part was no surprise for us. We knew he could do that, and we expected Val to do it.","\"What took us off guard was what he burned.\" She conjured a hologram of Althika’s and Erkin’s wounded life forces. \"Val’s Life Flames consumed the scar tissue and the lingering energy of your Dread Flames to feed and nurture mother and son back to health, including the dormant Divine Beasts’ aspects.","\"Yet what truly shocked us was the Life Flames forming a temporary bridge between Erkin’s life forces to empower them and feeding his dormant Divine Beast aspects no less than the dominant sides.\"","\"Wait, what?\" Lith’s eyes narrowed.","\"You heard her, Featherling.\" Salaark said. \"Erkin’s Dragon and Phoenix bloodlines are now easier to awaken than they were before the treatment. In other words, once Val grows in strength and skill, he might become capable of helping any hybrid to harmonize their life forces.\"","\"That’s amazing!\" Solus said.","\"That’s terrifying!\" Lith snorted. \"What Val did with the Camellia was already absurd. If what Grandma said is right, he will have to hide this ability for the rest of his life or become the target of every Awakened bloodline on Mogar!\"","\"What are you talking about? What does the fake magical flower have to do with any of this?\" Baba Yaga asked in confusion. \"Are you telling me this isn’t the first time the little imp did something this outrageous?\"","\"It’s easier if we show you.\" Solus Warped them to the Greenhouse, where Baba Yaga gasped at the sight of the living Camellia.","When she examined the flower, she stumbled a couple of steps back and fell to the ground.","\"Why?\" She asked, shapeshifting into her Mother form to tower over Solus and express the full extent of her outrage. \"Why didn’t you tell me sooner?\"","\"It’s just a flower-\"","\"This is not just a flower!\" Baba Yaga snarled. \"This is the result of the manipulation of a life force to such a deep level that I have no words to describe it. Show me how it happened.\"","She extended her hand, and Solus shared her memories of the events at Mogar’s Garden via a mind link.","\"This is preposterous!\" The Mother said. \"I would need months of research and experiments to achieve something like this, and you’re telling me a toddler did it on his first try?\"","\"Yes.\" Tyris said, brimming with pride.","\"Order and Chaos!\" Baba Yaga conjured a chair and plopped on it, muttering, \"Order and Chaos.\"","An awkward silence fell over the room while the Guardians played it cool and the Verhens realized how shallow their understanding of Valeron’s feat was.","***","In the following days, Althika got acquainted with the members of the Verhen family, keeping Aran and Leria for last. Unlike the triplets and the babies, they were old enough to know Trion couldn’t possibly have an offspring.","They greeted and treated the Titania politely, but accepting Meln’s son as one of their own was as difficult as it was for their parents.","To make matters worse, Lith, Solus, and Baba Yaga had to make four more travels. Lotho had spared the Redleaf Household no humiliation after teaching them a hard lesson about actions and consequences.","He shared everything he had learned about the Vurdalak bloodline with the rest of the Council and the risk that carrying one of Orpal’s children entailed. Alas, it was already too late.","By the time Lith arrived, two Dryads had already completely turned into Vurdalaks and assimilated their own child. The only thing left to do was to put them down and make sure that no trace of Orpal’s accursed blood remained.","A Titania, instead, resisted the hunger but failed to suppress the Light Soul. She became a full-blooded Vurdalak and managed to hold onto her sanity by the skin of her teeth.","Lith and Baba Yaga pooled their resources and knowledge, but there was no solution. The Titania’s original life force was gone, devoured by the Vurdalak blood. There was nothing she could return to, and destroying her Vurdalak life force would also kill her.","To make matters worse, the baby in her womb couldn’t survive without the mother.","\"Just end me!\" She begged amid tears and roars as Orpal’s fragment demanded that she fight Lith to the death. \"If you don’t, sooner or later I’ll hurt my child. Please, kill me while I’m still myself. Let me die like a Titania instead of a monster!\"","With great pain and a heavy heart, Lith made sure they died without pain.","\"This could have been avoided.\" Lith snarled, fighting the impulse to declare war on the Bloomriver clan. \"If only you called me sooner, they would still have been alive.\"","Arghul the Redcap bowed his head but said nothing. The Bloomriver clan had refused to believe Lotho’s warnings, thinking it was a ruse of the Council to smoke out Orpal’s children and keep plant and human Awakened bloodlines from achieving the power of a Divine Beast."]},{"number":4524,"title":"Chapter 4524 Coveted Bloodline (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Moreover, they believed that if Lith really had a cure, they could find one as well.","\"Verhen hates his brother and must have destroyed the baby’s Vurdalak life force to avoid competition. Wouldn’t we have done the same?\" Arghul had said, and everyone had agreed with him. \"The power of the Dead King is no different from magic.","\"We must only learn how to harness it, and everything will be fine. We’ll call Verhen only if everything else fails.\" The Bloomriver clan’s arrogance and lust for power led to the Titania’s tragic ending.","The fourth woman, Baryl, belonged to a human bloodline. The dreadful news scared one of its youngest members, who revealed her location and called for help. The problem was that neither the Galnorn Household nor Baryl wanted Lith’s help.","\"Cilgan is insane. There’s no one carrying the Dead King’s blood here!\" Pelnat, the clan head, said behind the cover of the magical formations.","\"How do you explain this, then?\" Lith showed a video of Baryl’s torment and the flames hovering above her head and womb. \"How do you explain this piece of cloth carrying the stench of a Upyr?\"","\"This is my home, and I don’t have to explain anything to you!\" Pelnat snarled. \"Ask Cilgan since he has all the answers.\"","\"Let me talk with the woman in the video, Baryl Galnorn.\" Lith replied. \"I won’t leave until I’m sure she’s alright.\"","\"As you wish, but I expect your apologies before you rid us of your presence.\" Pelnat took out her communication amulet and said something the arrays covered.","\"It’s useless.\" Cilgan whispered from Lith’s side. \"I tried to convince Baryl many times, but she’s not willing to relinquish her newfound powers.\"","\"It might be her, but it might be just Meln talking.\" Lith replied. \"He won’t be able to hold himself back if he sees me. It should snap Baryl out of her delusion of control and push her to ask my help.\"","\"Here I am, Verhen.\" Baryl appeared on the parapet, her face a mask of focus and determination.","Her skin was taut and covered in sweat from the effort of suppressing her Upyr side and hiding Light Soul’s flame. Lith used every means at his disposal to check on her life force, but from that distance, the magical formation clouded his mystical senses.","\"I’m fine, and I don’t need your help.\" Baryl lied through her teeth. \"I’m here of my own will, and no one is holding me prisoner.\"","\"Don’t be foolish, child!\" Baba Yaga said. \"Just say the word, and I’ll rescue you. Don’t believe their lies. The Galnorn Household’s arrays are nothing to me. I can protect you and your child, and your so-called family can’t do anything to stop me.\"","\"I appreciate your offer, Red Mother, but I don’t need to be rescued.\" Baryl said, and the Crone realized the woman truly believed it. \"As for you, Verhen, you have my pity. Going so far as to chase groundless rumors to keep the power of your bloodline for yourself.","\"It makes one wonder if the Vurdalak bloodline is as terrible as you say or if you’re just scared of its potential.\" Her arrogant smirk as she turned around and left told Lith everything he needed to know about Baryl Galnorn.","\"She really believes that nonsense.\" Lith spat those words like curses. \"She’s so full of herself that she thinks herself better than anyone else. That woman is the closest thing to a female Orpal I’ve ever seen.\"","\"Her willpower would be admirable if it weren’t just willfulness.\" Baba Yaga replied. \"She managed to suppress both her Upyr side and Orpal’s fragment, but it only emboldened her unbridled arrogance. There is no reasoning with her. She won’t ask for our help until it’s too late.\"","\"I’m waiting on those apologies!\" Pelnat’s smirk revealed where Baryl got her attitude from.","\"I’m sorry.\" Lith gave the Galnorns a deep bow. \"I’m really sorry it has to be this way.\"","He took a few steps back, and the Crone stepped forward.","\"Normally, I’d say watch and learn, child, but there’s nothing to be proud of in what I’m about to do. Besides, I’m quite certain you’d do it anyway.\" Baba Yaga tapped into Bloodhaven and extended her right hand, conjuring a spell like Lith had never seen before.","The ground beneath her feet trembled and cracked, and the spring breeze first turned into a strong wind and then into a tornado that descended from the sky onto the Galnorn Household.","Rivers of magma gushed from the depths of Mogar while every shadow turned into a pool of poison and every sunbeam into a sword of light.","’By my Mom!’ Solus had a hard time believing the reading of the Eyes. ’Malyshka isn’t controlling the power of the elements contained in the world energy. She’s controlling the elements that comprise Mogar itself!","’All the primordial forces are submitting to her will like well-trained dogs!’","’That’s-’ Lith was about to express his incredulity when the earth itself rose and crushed the earth-sealing arrays. ’Amazing!’","Baba Yaga’s White Core spell, Calamity End, tore the Galnorn Household’s magical defenses apart like paper and reached the grey stone fortress in seconds. The spell conjured localized natural disasters that no magic Lith knew could resist.","It was akin to fighting the planet itself, and no human, beast, or plant folk could ever be up to the challenge. The fortress collapsed like a house of cards when the Crone raised her hand, and the power of the elements crushed what was left in a vise when she closed her fist.","\"Cilgan.\" Her voice snapped the young man out of his terrified daze, making him flinch. \"You’re all that’s left of your bloodline, so I made sure not to destroy the treasure vault. You are going to need it to rebuild your Household, but first you need to move it to safety.","\"Be quick, because once Lith and I leave, I expect lots of scavengers to rush here and try to rob you blind. Only the strong can own riches. If you hold more than you can protect, you’re just begging to be robbed.\"","As she spoke, Lith used his enhanced sense of smell to spot the scent of Upyr blood amid the piles of debris and locate what was left of Baryl’s corpse.","’I’m sorry, kid. I really am. Neither of your parents deserved you.’ A burst of Dread Flames erased every trace of the corpses, leaving nothing behind that might have been studied and used to replicate the monstrosity that the Vurdalak was.","Before returning home, Lith visited Althika in the Desert to report to her the fate of her fellow members of Orpal’s harem. She had played a vital role in the search, helping Lith to identify the four women from their holograms and ensuring he wasn’t being used as a tool in the rivalry among Awakened bloodlines.","\"Am I really the only one who made it alive?\" She asked in shock, using her breathing technique to check on her baby in fear.","\"Yes.\" Lith nodded, his head low. \"It wasn’t much, but I did all I could. I was too late to save the Dryads and the Titania, and the human woman didn’t trust me enough to believe me.\"","\"Who, Baryl?\" The Titania’s lips curled up in disgust."]},{"number":4525,"title":"Chapter 4525 Constant Improvement (Part 1)","paragraphs":["\"Don’t waste your pity on her.\" Althika snorted. \"Baryl was a cheeky, insufferable minx who believed herself better than anyone else. She deserved everything she’s got coming to her.\"","\"Maybe, but her child didn’t.\" Lith sighed. \"Are you sure that’s all of them?\"","\"I’m sure.\" She replied. \"If Orpal- I mean, Meln got more women after I left, it’s impossible to say. I’m sorry.\"","\"Thanks anyway.\" Lith nodded.","’The old me would have thought the silver lining is that there’s no more spawn of Meln I have to take care of, but now I know better. There is no silver lining here, just the senseless shedding of innocent blood.’","’We did all we could, Lith.’ Solus gave him a telepathic embrace. ’There is no saving those who don’t want to be saved.’","’I know, but it’s a meager consolation. I wish I could’ve done more.’ Lith returned to the Mansion after checking on Erkin and the Titania.","Althika’s life force had completely recovered after her evolution, and Erkin wasn’t so afraid of strangers anymore. He didn’t recoil from Lith’s mana and welcomed it as he did with his mother’s.","That was the only silver lining in all that misery. After Lith freed the unborn baby from the curse of the Vurdalak and the Life Flames from pain, Erkin’s simple mind quickly forgot it and started to relish his peaceful existence.","\"How did it go?\" Kamila asked when Lith and Solus walked through the Mansion’s Warp Gate.","\"Like usual.\" Lith shook his head. \"There was nothing I could do.\"","Baba Yaga had preceded him and informed his family about the events so that Lith didn’t have to shoulder that burden on top of what he already carried. Kamila knew the answer to her question, yet she asked anyway to allow Lith to vent.","She waited for him alone to spare him from having to see the pain on his parents’ faces when he recounted the fate of their unborn grandchildren. This way, Lith didn’t have to explain himself or feel judged for his actions.","He was free to answer Kamila’s single question however he wanted, and she never pried further.","\"I’m so sorry.\" Kamila hugged him tightly and didn’t let go of him until he asked her to. \"How are you doing, Solus?\"","\"Like crap.\" She sniffled, returning Kamila’s hug. \"I’m glad I never had to leave my stone ring, but gods if it hurts. Those damn idiots...\"","She shook her head, unable to finish the phrase or withstand the memories those words would evoke.","\"Can you please let out Mom, Lith? I need a really long hug, and I don’t want to hog Kami to myself until next week.\"","\"Oh, right.\" Lith conjured his Sigil Demons, and for the first time he hesitated to look Trion in the eyes.","\"I’m sorry you had to do that, Little Brother.\" Trion patted Lith’s back as he walked out of the keep. \"I wish I had Dread Flames and could dirty my hands in your place. If you need me for anything, you know where to find me.\"","The two brothers weren’t close enough to support each other, so Trion preferred to leave that role to those Lith loved and trusted.","\"It’s not your fault, My Liege.\" Locrias said. \"Most of the time we wield our blades to protect those who can’t protect themselves, and a few sad times we wield them to do what no one else can or wants to do. It’s part of the job.\"","\"Mom, I...\" Solus sobbed, hugging Menadion with all her considerable strength.","\"Cry all you want, baby.\" The First Ruler of the Flames Warped them both to Solus’ room. \"Let everything out. You don’t want Ely, Val, and Ral to see you like this, do you?\"","\"No!\" Solus bawled her eyes out.","Meanwhile, in the keep, the silence stretched awkwardly.","\"Do you want to go see the babies?\" Kamila asked. \"I’m sure they’d cheer you up.\"","\"And if they ask me to use the Dragon Scales, I’ll scare them to death, Kami.\" He sighed. \"I’m sorry, but I need a minute.\"","\"Do you want me to leave?\" She knew nothing she could say or do would have lessened his burden one bit.","\"Please, stay here with me.\" Lith held her tight, feeling her warmth and listening to her steady heartbeat. \"I don’t want to talk, but I can’t bear to be alone.\"","They remained like that for a while, and without a tear shed, they cried.","***","As Lith cleansed the Vurdalak bloodline from the face of Garlen, Jorl kept himself busy in Verendi. Every time a fragment of Orpal’s consciousness died, he became temporarily weaker, and so did the corrupted life force in the Storm Griffon’s chest.","When that happened, he rushed back to the Black Throne as soon as he could and underwent another stabilization procedure. With each experiment, the cursed tower learned more about Jorl’s condition and adjusted his Body Sculpting spell to better suppress the Vurdalak life force.","The Griffon side also managed to reclaim more flesh with every session, but even on the fourth time it didn’t amount to much.","\"Are there more of Orpal’s bastards around?\" The Black Throne asked.","\"Not that I’m aware of.\" The Storm Griffon sighed. \"The escape of the first batch was a huge blow to his ego, and the liability the runaway women posed convinced him to keep it in his pants.","\"Or rather, to always use a birth control spell, but that limited his choice of partners greatly, which was an even bigger blow to his ego.\"","\"Good for him, but not for us.\" The cursed tower said. \"We didn’t salvage even half of the flesh you’ve lost, and if you’re right, we won’t get to perform another recovery treatment.\"","\"What truly matters is that I almost feel no pain and that my Upyr side is under control. Because it is under control, right?\" Jorl asked.","\"It is, but as long as the Dead King draws breath, you’ll never be safe.\" The Black Throne replied. \"I’m not Verhen. I can’t free you from the madness of the Vurdalak.\"","\"Then we act, and we do it fast.\" The Storm Griffon nodded. \"I’ve already asked my Upyrs to keep their eyes and ears open. If there’s so much as a rumor about Dawn’s current location, we’ll know it.\"","\"I’ve spread my word to my contacts as well. If they find her, they’ll let us know.\" The cursed tower said.","\"Since when do you have contacts?\" Jorl asked in surprise.","\"Since the beginning of time, apprentice.\" The Black Throne’s laugh was hoarse and dry. \"Cursed objects, mortals who crave my power, and others who believe me an eccentric mage are scattered across Mogar.","\"It’s only a matter of time before the Bright Day is in the palm of our hand.\"","***","A few days of peace and the constant improvement of Erkin’s condition uplifted Lith’s spirit a lot. Spending time with his loved ones and children did the rest.","\"I don’t care what people say about Dhiral, I think you’re going to be the next god of healing, Val.\"","\"Thanks, Daddy!\" The young boy had no idea what the title meant, but he giggled at the compliment nonetheless."]},{"number":4526,"title":"Chapter 4526 Constant Improvement (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Wah?\" Elysia asked in shock. \"Wadda abod me?\"","\"Good question, Ely. Any ideas about what you want to do when you grow up?\" Lith asked with a straight face, and the baby girl pondered the question for a while before forgetting it.","\"Are you excited to meet Auntie Zor again, Ral?\" Kamila asked.","\"Mama!\" He replied.","\"That’s the spirit.\" She chuckled. \"Say that a few times, please.\"","\"Yeah, we have a bet to settle.\" Solus said.","A few seconds later, what looked like a large black cloud appeared on the horizon and approached the Mansion at breakneck speed. Lith received Zoreth’s identification signal and lowered the arrays to let her in.","The Shadow Dragon landed with the grace of a sparrow and the lightness of a fluffy cloud. Her feet made no sound when they touched the ground, and her body rose in a pillar of black smoke that quickly compressed itself into the figures of two human women.","Or rather, one human woman and a humanoid woman.","\"How are my cuties?\" Zoreth was in her Arke form, with her four arms extended for a hug. \"You have no idea how much your auntie missed you.\"","\"I could have used a bit less smoke, Zor.\" Bytra, the Raiju and Fourth Ruler of the Flames, coughed up the foggy bits of her wife that had remained stuck in her throat.","\"And I could use a bit less nagging, Byt!\" The Arke’s four eyes frowned in annoyance. Her dull blue skin emphasized the expression lines on her face. \"Progress, not perfection.\"","\"Auie Soeed! Auie Soeed!\" Elysia jumped off Solus’ arms and landed into Zoreth’s.","\"You’ve learned another letter of my name!\" The Arke peppered the baby girl’s head with kisses. \"You’re such a smart girl, Ely.\"","\"Yah!\" Elysia giggled with pride.","\"And who is this annoying hag, instead?\" Zoreth pointed at Bytra.","\"Zor!\" The Raiju blushed in embarrassment.","\"No, Auie Bida!\" Elysia waved her index finger.","\"Sorry, Byt, Elysia agrees with me.\" The Arke chuckled.","\"That’s not what she- never mind.\" Bytra crossed her arms and pouted.","\"Hi, Auntie Zor.\" Valeron leaned toward her, and Zoreth hugged him with her second set of arms.","\"Gods, you’ve gotten big, Val. You’re almost as handsome as your dad now.\" She kissed his forehead and ruffled his hair.","\"Since Zor is hogging Val and Ely, I’ll take Ral if that’s okay with you.\" Bytra grunted.","\"Sure, just handle him with caution.\" Kamila handed the baby boy over. \"You know how dangerous he is.\"","\"Dangerous? But if he’s a cutie! Isn’t that right, Ral?\" Bytra took the boy in her arms and held him tight to her chest.","\"Mama!\" Raldarak took her hand and nuzzled against it.","\"Gods!\" Bytra’s heart tightened as if a vise were squeezing it, and her knees turned into jelly. \"I need to sit down.\"","\"Mama?\" Ral asked with a worried look in his big, round eyes.","\"No, I’m not your mom, but I’d kill to be her.\" Bytra’s legs went out, and she fell to the ground, sobbing.","Raldarak tried to console her by kissing her tears away, but the Raiju just cried harder.","’Told you. Twice is more than enough.’ Solus said via a mind link. ’Pay up, Kami.’","’Not a chance. We still have Zoreth to even the score.’ Kamila replied.","\"Byt!\" Zoreth handed the babies back and helped her wife to stand up. \"Stop embarrassing us. You know that Ral calls everybody mama, and that’s what makes him dangerous.\"","\"I know, but I can’t help myself.\" She gave the baby boy to Zoreth.","\"Mama!\" Raldarak gave the Arke a bright smile that could have lightened up the entire Lustria County.","\"Gods!\" Zoreth bawled her eyes out, holding the baby as if he were her long-lost son.","’Dammit!’ Solus inwardly cursed. ’So much for a millennia-old Eldritch. She was supposed to last at least three mamas!’","’We’ll call this even.’ Kamila replied as she offered several handkerchiefs to her guests.","\"I told you to handle him with care.\" She actually said. \"Do you want me to take Ral away?\"","\"NO!\" The two women screamed in unison, shielding the boy with their bodies and conjuring their best spells.","\"Do you remember I’m his mother and not a kidnapper, right?\" Kamila would have found the situation hilarious if not for the constant struggle to keep her own son.","\"Oh.\" The hybrids exchanged a glance that proved they had actually forgotten about it.","\"I’m sorry, Kami. I don’t know what’s gotten into me.\" Zoreth said, taking a step back for good measure.","\"I do.\" Kamila grunted. \"It’s the same thing that gets into every woman who holds Ral and gets called mama.\"","\"That’s not true!\" Bytra said, eyeing the best escape route for her wife and the baby.","\"Stop looking for the best escape route, and I’ll believe you.\" Kamila snarled. \"Give me my baby back, please.\"","Zoreth reluctantly returned Raldarak, looking at Kamila as if she were a heartless monster.","\"Congratulations, Big Sis.\" Lith stepped forward, eclipsing the baby boy and snapping the Arke out of her maternal fever. \"I see you’ve learned how to shapeshift into your humanoid form on your own.\"","\"Lith?\" Zoreth suddenly remembered where she was and why. \"I mean, thanks, Lil Bro. It took me a lot of work, but the more my troll side stabilized, the more my affinity to the light element grew.","\"With a bit of study, I’ve become an excellent healer and learned how to hear the melody of a life force. At that point, turning into an Arke was child’s play. It’s one of the many reasons I came to visit you aside from the pleasure of your company, Lil Bro.\"","\"Bytra.\" Solus gave the Raiju a polite nod and offered her to hold Ely and Val.","\"Solus.\" Bytra cleared her throat. \"How are you and these adorable little imps doing?\"","\"Auie Bida! Auie Bida!\" Elysia stared at the Ruler of the Flames, wondering why only her little brother stirred such intense emotions in their aunties.","\"Ely, Val!\" The Raiju held both kids with ease, kissing their cheeks and foreheads. \"Gods, you’ve gotten so big. Ely is already a beautiful lady and Val a handsome boy.\"","Without Dragon Scales, Bytra couldn’t understand the baby girl’s question, and even if she did, she would never have answered it because it would lead to more embarrassing questions and answers.","\"De yu!\" Elysia giggled, while Valeron blushed a bit.","\"Sorry, Byt. Elysia replaced the second b with a d, but I got that too, plus the extra right letter of my name. I’m the winner this time.\" Zoreth said.","\"That’s just because you have a longer name.\" The Fourth Ruler of the Flames snorted. \"Isn’t that right, Val?\"","\"Yes, Auntie Bytra.\" The young boy nodded. \"Auntie Zoreth has a longer name.\"","\"See?\" Bytra puffed her chest out with pride, making Elysia wonder for the umpteenth time what the point of sporting such a generous size just to be a dry well was.","\"What do you mean, many reasons?\" Lith asked.","\"I came here to show you the progress I made in developing my life forces and ask you to check on them with the Infirmary, but we have a few things to discuss.\" Zoreth replied. \"I’ve heard about your latest feat, Lil Bro.\""]}]);
